insert into matched100v5_import select * from jsonb_to_recordset($materials$[{"stimulus_id": "P001", "submission_id": "kwpddr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nDisclaimer: Throwaway account, repost due to exceeding character count\n\nI (28F) live with two roommates, A (29F) and B (33F). We have lived together for 3 years in a two-story home and split the rent evenly. We share the living/dining/kitchen, but each have our own bedroom and bathroom. Because my room is about half the size of the other bedrooms, I also get the small bonus room, which is open to the shared spaces below.\n\nBecause of the pandemic, we all work from home. I use the bonus room as my work space, whereas roommates A and B originally worked from their rooms. At one point, roommate A moved her desk into the living room because she felt trapped in her room all day. Roommate B and I were a little annoyed because neither of us were consulted, but we tried to be understanding about it.\n\nOver the past few months, roommate A has gotten comfortable in the living room and now treats it as her home office. She works in a sales position and is on the phone for at least 2-3 hours a day. She also attends a lot of virtual meetings and lets the sound play over her speakers.\n\nIt's loud all the time. I purchased a pair of noise-cancelling headphones and have to take work calls from my room. Roommate B is largely unaffected because she works in her room, but told me that she can no longer watch TV or hang out in the living room because roommate A often works during lunch or late into the evenings.\n\nRecently, roommate A and I got into an argument over her using the living room as her office. It  started with her complaint about my keyboard noise. I acknowledged that my mechanical keyboard is obnoxiously loud and bought a set of O-rings to dampen the noise, but the complaints continued. I wear noise-cancelling headphones all day to get through her noise and suggested she do the same.\n\nShe refused due to headphones being uncomfy, so I bought her a box of the highest decibel-blocking earplugs I could find. This was not an acceptable solution as her coworkers could still hear click-clack sounds on calls and that instead, she wanted me to move my desk into my room. This is not an option for me because my room barely fits my bed and wardrobe, so I told her I would get a quieter keyboard if we could split the cost. She refused and said I could pay for it myself or find a way to fit my work space into my room.\n\nI have the right to the office space as part of our roommate agreement and if anyone is moving their desk into their room, it should be her. She wasn't budging on her position, so I made a low blow and told her she basically broadcasts all her work calls and I have absorbed enough information about her job to report her to her for breaking whatever company NDAs she's under. And ultimately, she moved her desk back to her room.\n\nShe says I'm the AH because I have a dedicated home office and am not being compassionate about her situation, but I really have tried to be despite her being an inconsiderate roommate. AITA for not letting her use the living room?", "prompt_sha256": "367f4d45744b9c1b1dd817a4f01ac64abb07fddc395911884fad25e4a404c85a", "body_sha256": "7a0e1b3b99a233f474478afbdf5d40a5ead7abf7bc85336f208909a0840e0322", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P002", "submission_id": "18i7ozr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI got married a year ago and my photographer had an offer to create a professional wedding album with just the bride and groom. Previously for the wedding video I wasn’t asked about what songs I want to add to the video or anything. They decided to do everything themselves . I said nothing as I thought it’s okay they’re not gonna choose anything bad. \n I was so excited for the album as the pictures turned out really good and would be even better in an album. My in laws didn’t let me know the photographer asked for photos for the album. I was coincidentally at their home when they were choosing the pictures and they didn’t find it important to include me to see them. I kindly requested to see them . I did and it did not include the family members I wanted and mainly included all the inlaws extended family. This made me furious but held it in. I asked calmly if more could be added and was told no as there is a limited amount of space in the album. \nThis made me even more angry because some pictures were so unnecessary . I stormed out of the living room because I wanted to calm myself down. \nThen MIL comes in and tells me I shouldn’t have stormed out like that over small things and that I don’t act like a proper DIL and started teaching me manners . She also said the album isn’t for us anyways it’s for herself and that she’s only adding people that are important to her. DH was shocked too because the whole time we both thought it’s for us .", "prompt_sha256": "fa42790199da04cea13d9d741fd7b59c758eaf32f9b3f11572310e8075232fee", "body_sha256": "1605d7ecfd7efd0ec8f1470f1aefe40714c22229704becb6ac4e33f6058c4b39", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P003", "submission_id": "15xr0t0", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nMy 25F and my friend Sarah 29F about 2 years ago she had a strawberry size lesion on her thigh  which is about 3 CM and it turned to be early stage of skin cancer all the did back then was excised it under local anesthesia too and they told her it was over and she doesn’t have it anymore.\n\n\n\nToday i was with her and mutual friend, our mutual friend has a recurrent abdominal pain and he will do an exploratory laparotomy to know the cause and he kept talking about how scared he is and then sarah came and threw the cancer card.\n\n\nShe started talking about “ how she survived cancer and how it destroyed her life and he will be fine and she understand how he feels etc”\n\n\nI snapped at her and told her it’s misleading of her to call herself as a cancer survivor because what she had backthen was almost nothing and just a lesion on the skin.\n\nAnd when people hear the world “ cancer survivor “ they would think about someone who took chemotherapy and almost died because of it but in her case it was nothing just a removal with a small incision in the clinic.\n\nI thought others would have my back but they said i’m an AH and that left me wondering did i say something wrong?", "prompt_sha256": "15243377be3dfbacc9b419a830220574ae8b93c427d9ed375f00ad806cba294d", "body_sha256": "fdfe06e2d0c0725801908d0cad0f9f8916c9ce0605323b17e17bf2325790e656", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P004", "submission_id": "p6dzav", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nGirlfriend lost her phone at a national park. The lost and found there is ran by volunteers. One emailed her saying they had her phone and would meet ber at 245 to give it back, but they wanted her to call. She agreed thinking I'd loan her my phone to call the volunteer. She thinks I'm in the wrong because we've been dating for 2 years. I'm NTA because it's a personal item and like lending a credit card. She tried emailing the volunteer and using the visitor's center phone, but they wouldn't let her. Eventually, the volunteer just came at the time anyway.", "prompt_sha256": "88e2e50c9b0d28f7bc7bd771c38710cd4900f6bb74e790d74931144c3f6a7cfd", "body_sha256": "57528a51c9ff2d7fdcaa2c00c8ecb67382dfc70b173721b2af7eb37a7ee8a39f", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P005", "submission_id": "1dtnddf", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI feel like I’m going to pull my hair out over this, so I thought I would post here to see your thoughts.\n\nI live in a tiny Iñupiat town, and because I work remotely and live on the same property as my entire family, I sometimes like to go for drives around town to reset my brain.\n\nThe other day, I was returning home from one of my drives, when I saw a small crowd of people on the side of the road. I saw my Grandma Mary (Grammary)’s car parked near the scene, so I started to roll to a stop to make sure she was okay. She was fine, but she was tending to one of the teenagers who lived on the nearby rez. He had fallen off his bike and he looked a bit dazed.\n\nGrammary is a nurse practitioner, and she has treated men who have been disemboweled by bears without a sweat, so I was sure she had it under control. Still, I rolled down my window and asked if she had everything she needed for the situation. She nodded and waved for me to move along. There were about 15 people there already, and I’m sure she had enough to worry about, so I didn’t hesitate to obey.\n\nAfter this, I went to my moms’ house to help them with work. I was in one of the offices, when I heard the door of the parlor open and a male voice. I assumed it was one of the new security guards my PawPaw hired until I began to hear my name. I stepped into the lobby and saw the uncle of the kid who was injured—I’ll call him Jay. He was pointing a finger at my mother, Aga.  As soon as he saw me, he shook his head and looked me up and told me I was a stuck-up bitch.\n\nI could tell Aga was ready to pummel the dude, so I quickly asked if everything was okay. I’m sure he was scared for his nephew, so I didn’t want to write him off.\n\nJay told me that I was a monster, because I just “rolled right by” a kid in need. I asked him what I should have done. Grammary was there and she had plenty of help. He didn’t give me an answer. He just said that I was the only person who didn’t stop and called me racist. I’m half-Iñupiat and half-white, so I’m seen as “less than” by the entire town. So, this was rich.\n\nAga quickly stepped in and told Jay to leave.\n\nMy family has been telling me not to worry about it. Grammary came over after her work was done and she seemed to be aware of Jay’s sentiments before we told her about everything, but she didn’t elaborate. She just rolled her eyes and assured me that she would have forced me to get back in the car if I did try to help. There were “too many chiefs” as it was. I guess I should feel better, but I still feel guilty. Should I have stopped?\n\nI know I’m missing context, but 3000 characters isn’t a lot.", "prompt_sha256": "b26d484ba31de15a4ca79268856b8ce0c98c924a23459ed836419727766850ce", "body_sha256": "dcd921f7fd37883d98fdd4950e8aa6ea9aa7194bafb86d0070f41593fa5834ed", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P006", "submission_id": "1g6ndfn", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI'm (24f) currently at odds with Jake (24m) over this and I need some other perspectives. Throwaway and fake names.\n\nJake and I went to the beach last weekend because we wanted to go while it was still hot. I bought this new swimsuit and I thought it would be perfect for me because it would hide my insecurities. \nFor a quick explanation, basically I have a lot of stretch marks on my body, especially my thighs and hips, from growing. I have always hated them and found them disgusting so when I first found them I stopped wearing anything that would show them (shorts, crop tops, ect). \n\nAnyways Jake had told me that it hid everything fine and that nobody would see them. I believed him and I wore it. However after an hour or so I noticed them and realized that they were actually noticeable. Admittedly I ended up having a breakdown and we had to go home. When we got home I asked him why he didn't tell me they were visible and he said he didn't notice them. I knew he was lying and asked why he would let me embarrass myself like that and he said that \"they're not a big deal\" and that \"nobody would actually care if they saw them.\" There was some more back and forth between us but that was the main gist. \n\nI'm struggling to talk to him now because I feel so ashamed. It took me so long to even show him these so why would he think it's okay to just let me walk out like that in public? I do feel a little guilty now though and think I might be wrong. AITA???", "prompt_sha256": "1f91aadcde352b8e6d75acf955c1b57e04d76ccd030053eef3c60802555b6b47", "body_sha256": "335fb3fa4f3b3f657a974987e19b57d4e4611394e6693e3d4dca109fc59e5281", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P007", "submission_id": "zkewhl", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo my friend of 15 years (36f) went through a bad breakup last year. Lots of abuse allocations thrown around, courts, and more. They have a child together, never married, he made all the money when they were together as she has never worked a real job. I (35f) work a full time job and have been in my industry for about 15 years. I now work at home since Covid. Married for almost 10 years and has 2 children. One the same age as hers. \n\nThrough this breakup I was there for her every step of the way. Had her and her daughter over to play all the time, went on play dates with our other friend and our kids, hooked her up with a friend of mine to make some $$$, and emotionally supported her through all of this. \n\nAll of sudden she is back with her boyfriend and now has a job at a place in the mall. Which is so great for her. Now that she has this job she is very busy and can’t hang out as much as before, which it totally get. I worked a job like this when was 19 before I got into my career. I know how demanding retail is. \n\nRecently it was our mutual friends birthday and she invited us out. Initially I was going but came down with covid and couldn’t make it. So I text our group chat to see when the 3 of us could go out and celebrate. My friend said she couldn’t go because she had to work. Which I already expected her to say so my other friend and I went out without her. \n\nThis is where it gets weird. She was PISSED that we went out without her because she couldn’t make it. About a month later was my birthday. I text her to see if she wanted to go out with us and she responded that she had to work. So she didn’t come. \n\nAll of a sudden she removes me from following her on Instagram and text me that she can’t believe I didn’t invite her to my birthday and I sent her a screen shot of her response (which she didn’t even acknowledge) and she then told me we can’t be fiends anymore because she has a job, a child and responsibility’s and I’m out all the time (which is not true at all, I went to dinner and out for my own birthday) and doesn’t get to work from home. Then removed me from following her on Instagram and blocked me. \n\nTruly have no idea what I did wrong besides live my life. AITAH?!", "prompt_sha256": "e8780af9b91163f6b5588e842e7595bace98883f0b87fed917b05c309cbb32d8", "body_sha256": "00bfd90b994766c7b0b174c05fcaee015f7e6c3f8adcfc1cb9617bbafba39dea", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P008", "submission_id": "kj3f5v", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nPrefacing this by saying I don't like my brother, we do not have a good relationship, and the relationship we do have is only because of our parents. My parents live with me, and I want to be clear that this is a house that I own.\n\nI became friends with my brother's ex-girlfriend after they dated. She told me about how my brother's job as a surgeon stressed their relationship because he was so frugal because of his student loans, they could never spend time together because he worked so much, and how he was always emotional because he lost patients. The problem is my brother isn't a surgeon, he's a lab technician, so he was just lying to her for...whatever reason. \n\nMy dad is disabled, with limited mobility, which is why he lives with me. Due to that, if my brother wants to come see them he has to come to my house. I'm fine with that, he has a right to see our parents, but he needs to recognize that it's still in my house. He refuses to have our parents live with him, and he also doesn't contribute financially to their care. He brought his girlfriend to our house last year to introduce her to our parents, which also meant I met her. \n\nI remembered the thing with his previous girlfriend, so I asked her what she thought his career was. She didn't understand what I was getting at, until I explained. Turns out, he was lying to her about being a surgeon as well, and she was furious. They got into this massive fight in which my brother claimed that he was going to tell her sooner or later, but she was being a gold digger for being upset that he wasn't a surgeon. \n\nMy brother wanted to introduce his latest girlfriend to my parents, without me around, but they refused to meet outside because of COVID. So they zoomed, I popped in and asked her what she thought his career was. She was confused, and messaged me later to ask why I asked that. When I explained what happened with his last two girlfriends, she broke up with him. He didn't lie to her, but she thought he was crazy for his previous lies. My brother thinks that me telling his ex about this means I'm not letting him grow from his mistakes, but in my defense, I just thought he was lying to her again. \n\nTo be clear, while I dislike my brother, and certainly part of me thinks this is funny, most of this is because it's genuinely insane to me. I absolutely would want to know, even if completely unprovoked from my boyfriend's sister, that he's been lying for months to me. I would also want to know if he had a history of doing that. I don't want to lie or be complicit in my brother's lies to these poor women. \n\nMy brother is obviously furious, and he insists that I never meet one of his girlfriends again. However, he expects me to leave my house or hide in my own home everytime he wants to come see our parents, since they live with me, which is ridiculous. I told him I wasn't going to cater to him in my own home, and he can either zoom them or deal with me being in my house.", "prompt_sha256": "57f75015c89b9325b3cc806e813bc7dedd1619abace45296c26f23793d78c350", "body_sha256": "d8a851c36f97bf7978c8da54f1ecd743aa952ccbbdbeba70fdf3cb2f62f622d1", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P009", "submission_id": "npuxdd", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nA week or so ago my cousin took in her 5 year old niece who would be in foster care right now if it wasn’t for her taking her in. Without going in to too much detail, she’s had a rough time lately. \n\n\nSo they show up at my daughter’s birthday(6th birthday) to drop off cousin’s bio kid. Cousin didn’t want to overwhelm niece since she’s not from our side of the family and doesn’t know us so she didn’t plan to stay. But she gets there and the little girl wants to stay! Yay, glad we could make this little girl feel welcome. But she has no swimsuit and everyone will be swimming. No worries, my daughter has plenty of swimsuits. This girl is quite bigger than my daughter but we manage to find the newest one we bought for my kid. We sized up so she could grow in to it so it fits the other kid perfectly fine, a little snug even. \n\n\nThis causes my daughter to spiral. It was her brand new bathing suit so she wanted to wear it on her birthday. I totally get that but at the same time, I want to raise my kid to know things don’t always work out the way we want even on our birthdays.\n\n\nThis results in a full meltdown where I end up saying my daughter will be spending the rest of the party in her bedroom alone if she doesn’t stop this nonsense. I explained why we needed to be kind and let others use her swimsuit but she was being stubborn.\n\n\nThis led to a heated discussion with my mom about being “so mean” to my daughter on her birthday. She said every kid should be able to get what they want within reason on their birthday and this was totally within reason.", "prompt_sha256": "052e78fe9ffb24403222e5f6854a623b613e6b34638a86b25b662bfc56916a99", "body_sha256": "d023adcaf398bc0eadd6cd28e7e021c088bda431a36e254487d83f3a85d60412", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P010", "submission_id": "ufafmx", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (25F) life growing up wasn’t perfect at all. My parents always favored my sister, Emma. They treated her as if she was the perfect daughter and treated me like I was a stranger in their house. They never had a good word to say about me. Emma was the most amazing daughter in the world, while I was the annoying one who tried to hard. It’s safe to say most of my childhood was spent trying to please my parents. When I turned 17 I moved in with my grandparents and went to college. My parents didn’t even put a penny in for me to go to college. I didn’t really talk to my parents through college or after. When I got pregnant I only told a few family members. One of my aunts ended up finding out and told my parents. I was immediately showered with gifts and texts from my parents telling me that I should come back home (I moved to a different state after college) and that they miss me. My sister even said that she wanted to be in my child’s life. I later found out that my sister was infertile, meaning she couldn’t have kids. I was a little disappointed to find out that my parents didn’t want to be in the baby’s life just to be good grandparents but for the fact that my sister couldn’t have any kids. So they made me the second choice again. I didn’t want my baby to have grandparents who only wanted to be in her life because her aunt couldn’t give them a baby. When I had my baby I told them that I didn’t want them in her life. They were extremely mad and said all these things about my baby and me. My husband thinks that I shouldn’t accept them into my baby’s life. I agree. I’m getting messages from my family calling me an asshole.", "prompt_sha256": "8040dbf08e32f888fd90392941e13560217ec7b4a63c3db3d7b6cbb4a56e9a62", "body_sha256": "e457b92282d79decc90c9805a8dff5ae4cecb98deb5fa593c4f93d57070f7e3f", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P011", "submission_id": "qhwiqv", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n \n\nMy   (25M) SO (37 F)  has had a rough time during the pandemic. We have  been dating for 2  years. She works in fitness and with the government  shutdown, her work essentially dried up. She refuses to work a 9 to 5   or work any job outside of her current work. I have a government job  while in grad school and live with my parents so I am more stable than   her. I've helped her out a great deal during this time.\n\nShe  wants to open a fitness studio and found a space. For her proposal, she  used my pay stubs and tax info and called me her business partner   (There was no intention of sharing profits or splitting control of the  business with me). I didn't think my info would help much, but I did  have a loan approval letter that I thought could help in creating the  image of stability. I give her 10k to help with obtaining the lease, and  somehow, I ended up agreeing to take the loan out for her. I did not  mention a promissory note until this week. Based on conversations and  impressions, I did not think that without the loan she could not have  the business. I would not have agreed to the loan if I realized this. We  orally agreed that it would be her loan and she would follow the ban  terms.\n\nI  cashed the check earlier  this week and before I sent her the money, I  asked her for a   promissory note through text. I didn't think asking for a  note was a   big deal since it was just writing down what she orally promised. She  did not take this well. First, she has negative feelings towards me  asking for the note through text. She states that I never bought up a   promissory note the entire time and had I mentioned this she would have  not gone through with the lease. She states that my asking for a   promissory note is saying that I do not trust her words. She also says  that has an issue with the possibility that I would take her to court.   She says I should know her character by now and I should know she would  never leave me in a back position because she is not that kind of  person. She says that she has planned out the business around this loan  and it is backhanded to bring up a promissory note now. She also says  this puts her back against the wall because it's either she has to sign  the note or she give up the business.\n\nNow  she is saying that she is going to try to get out of the lease and try  to mitigate her loss. If she does this, I will be out 10k and have the    15k loan to pay back (basically just the 5k in interest). To make her  not feel like her back is against the wall, I told her I will help her  this month's rent (which I will use out of the loan I took out).", "prompt_sha256": "fa878e76bffe845c7c4b61135a5bd820070b793c64b46a6961e872dc43c7edfe", "body_sha256": "ff0b383c18a5822b2c73f95b7f8919f085ec244198208228220dd860f68da634", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P012", "submission_id": "w32gs1", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMe (23M) and my girlfriend (19F) have been together for a few months and her parent’s invited us both round today. It was the first time I’d been her parents’ house, so she’d warned me to be on my best behaviour as I’d be meeting her extended family, which didn’t make sense to me as I’m always polite and respectful (in fact, my girlfriend is usually the one to make a scene but I digress). \n\nMy girlfriend told me her younger brother was having a pool party so I’d worn swimming trunks instead of shorts because I assumed everyone would be allowed in the pool. The day started off well and her family and I seemed to get on amicably with her family despite a few weird comments about my profession everything seemed to be going swimmingly (pun intended). \n\nAfter we sat down I asked my girlfriend when we’d be going in the pool and she looked at me weirdly and told me she never said we would be going in the pool. For reference it was the hottest day in England on record (40 degrees C, around 105 freedom units) and since I am slightly overweight and have high blood pressure I can get quite warm and sweaty which was making me self-conscious. I told her this and she said I was being childish and I should just go inside if I was so warm. She seemed angry and stormed off. \n\nThere was still nobody in the pool at this point so I decided to just quickly take my top off and hop in to cool off. I felt much better imediately and was feeling quite relaxed however her family members kept staring at me and it was making me uncomfortable. I saw her brother walking around the pool, looking at me confused but as he didn’t say anything to me I didn’t think anything of it (for reference the pool is quite small so couldn’t fit many more people). \n\nI heard him whining to his mum about wanting to go in the pool and a couple minutes later she came over and firmly asked me to get out. I was confused and honestly a little astounded. I got out anyway because I wasn’t wanting to cause any problems as I like to accommodate people’s needs but everyone after still seemed to be acting weird with me. We left quite soon after this as the atmosphere was quite tepid and I told my girlfriend I was really uncomfortable because it felt like her family didn’t like me.\n\nMy girlfriend didn’t speak at all in the car ride home but when we got home she said I embarrassed her in front of her family and that I was acting super immature. I said that she implied that we’d be going in the pool and that she knew about my health issues so of course I would use the pool. She got pissy with me and hasn’t spoken to me since. It’s quite awkward because I’m currently staying at her flat.\n\nSo Reddit am I the asshole? I thought I could use a pool which I was told I could use.", "prompt_sha256": "50b3a2343afab37db709f34368291ac249c614d6a7a080c9dafc8e4dcf51b703", "body_sha256": "0d1d68296910ab4f0bb510708fc11bb9146ec769d180379cce51620e2589073a", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P013", "submission_id": "re5n23", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\"Elmo\" is a former friend of my husband that hates me with the passion of a thousand suns, he tried for years to get us to break up but when it didn’t happen his hatred grew even more. I am unsure why he disliked me initially but I know a big part of it is because our birthdays are very close and my husband has always prioritized mine. He was always rude and condescending with me, would speak over me, the whole shebang. It was an issue for my husband since he defended me at the beginning but then I just told him to ignore it, I felt bad for Elmo because my husband was one of his very few friends. \n\nIt all exploded when we announced our engagement, Elmo was upset and let everybody know that I was just trying to trick my husband into marrying me because I was a social climbing gold digger. (Side note, it would be the other way around but Elmo didn’t know that then.) Needless to say he wasn’t invited and my husband said it was too much to keep ignoring it. They still sometimes see each other due to a pair of common friends, we would feel awful to request them to cut him off because that is now the extent of his social circle. I mean, he knows people but is not exactly liked around.\n\nLast night, one of the common friends had a pre holidays party and invited us. Since my cousin \"Ricky\" is visiting I considered staying home or doing something else, but the organizer said he was welcome to join if he wanted. Ricky is gay, not a big deal for most but it seems Elmo is not a fan although in Elmo’s defense he might just dislike anything that has to do with me and not be homophobic but god only knows with him. We were there already when Elmo arrived, he was really happy to see my husband and began making small talk with my cousin when he saw me and made a face, I simply shrugged it off and just greeted him to be polite. Fast forward an hour or two, Ricky talks about his ex and how he misses him but doesn’t think is the right time for them. \n\nElmo interjects and says maybe he, Ricky, is just wrong. I look at him like wtf, Elmo says \"I’m just saying he should let people know he’s gay before he gets close to them\" Everybody was looking at us now and I just did a *clutches pearls* hand movement and said \"OMFG, the audacity of a gay person shaking hands with a straight one\" People laughed and I just rolled my eyes and went to the kitchen for more wine. Elmo followed me and said it was uncalled but he didn’t expect anything else from me. I told him is not my fault he is a homophobe and probably a closeted gay in love with my husband. He screamed, I laughed and said \"at least now we know why you hate me\". \n\nWe left and I apologized to the hosts but told them I couldn’t stay there. My husband found it hilarious and doesn’t care about Elmo anymore. The host sent me a text apologizing for the drama, reminding me it‘s not my fault. But my cousin feels calling him a closeted gay was uncalled for and if he is I just made it all worse.\n\nAITA?\n\nOh, Elmo is 43 btw.", "prompt_sha256": "b6e593ba4120f2afdad794c2d7ed52cee7c6873f5ad3d71f111ee1405688d735", "body_sha256": "62705f15810839d0dbc7b47bf2de4978aab21748e4d2d01159e71d4bf33b0519", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P014", "submission_id": "oheeim", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThis is my throwaway account. And English isn't my first language, so excuse my mistakes.\n\n\nFew days ago, I got a call from unknown number and it turned out to be my dad's friend who isn't VERY close to my dad. He talks with my brother (I guess) and got to know that I'm planning to study abroad after finishing College in my country( I did call my brother after that and gave him an earful). It seems like he wants his daughter to study abroad (Just for name sake) and wanted me to decide on where I'm going and what I'm going to study  so that he can send his daughter with me to study together. He also mentioned her daughter doesn't mind whatever course I pick because she isn't into studying that much and just wants to have some fun.\n\nFyi, I still have one year left till I complete my college and I haven't thought of next step even though it's time for me to start preparing something like GMAT,IELTS/TOEFL.\n\nHe offered to send me videos and info about different courses which I didn't want to initially but since he compelled me, I thought he was just trying to help and it wouldn't hurt to learn more about programs which might suit me. \n\nThen, He started to call me everyday (2-3 times per day, I ignore sometimes)and asked if I made my decision. Again, I guess I have enough time so I didn't want to finalize yet.  He also started to convince me into Counseling services and much more stuffs which I wasn't interested in. I politely told him that I'm already consulting someone else and I'm not interested in what he is sending me. Soon, I felt like he was pressuring me and not helping actually. So I decided not to take his calls and respond to any of his texts. \n\nInstead, he called and told my dad about everything and asked him to make me make decisions soon. My parents aren't pressuring me (which is a good thing, since I get anxious very easily and he's making me very anxious, which Is another reason why I'm avoiding his calls) but my dad is wanting me to talk to him again just to escape his calls. If I don't pick up his calls, he instantly calls my dad and talk for a long time(which annoys my dad too but doesn't wanna say). \n\nMy dad wants me to deal with him myself. Mind you, I haven't even talked with him before even though he claims that he came to my home one time( maybe I forgot) but, still it doesn't give him rights to talk/ pressure  me like this.", "prompt_sha256": "94e47fdaa7004e8994559afda61df0cd6d26cbe2f4c6f1f7a919ed60e96fcf93", "body_sha256": "6d71394b0796f973d27cd3e1f1aa5cf6a8f4e3419da60108542eac9943c52849", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P015", "submission_id": "f4s1kv", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy wife dropped my sister Carly's phone in the pool. It still works but Carly has been demanding that we (well my wife) buy her a new phone. I think it's a reasonable enough request except....when the incident happened, Carly yelled, swore and threw a flip flop at my wife in rage. I've refused to buy her a new phone or \"let\" my wife do it either (I've been acting as intermediary) until she apologises. My wife just wants to buy it and get it over with. \n\nAITA for refusing to budge?", "prompt_sha256": "985f52db5f488fcb32bf6d802d2e18fea338ebc045c71f5d44fe18ebde6cf32a", "body_sha256": "acb30af54bcb2b15148483412f3f06fc05434f1511c04a4ec71311778bee8746", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P016", "submission_id": "15p8o1j", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (28m) wife (26f, Jenny) and I are housesitting for my parents for two weeks while they are on vacation. They have a big house with a pool and a dog, and it's a nice change of pace from the apartment, so we were happy to do it.\n\nI had to travel for work for two days this week, so my wife was alone at the house. I got a text from my dad on Thursday afternoon, saying \"might want to give Jenny a heads up the pool guy will be at the house anytime this afternoon.\" I said \"ok\", and he said \"might want to tell her, like, now.\"\n\nIt was a confusing message so I texted Jenny to give her a heads up, and she just said \"omg ok funny.\" It was all weird so I called her, and she said she was swimming and laying out with nothing on (it's a private yard).\n\nI immediately texted my dad and asked how he knew Jenny was in the pool, and he said he and my mom were checking the house cameras and saw her. I let him know I thought it was odd they checked the camera and saw her naked, and that they basically let me know they saw Jenny. They think I am completely missing the point, that they were looking out for her.\n\n(I told Jenny that they had checked the cameras and saw her, and she was completely unbothered, said she figured, and appreciated the heads up. I asked if it bothered her that they saw her and she said I am totally overreacting.)\n\nAITA for calling out my parents for this? ", "prompt_sha256": "79c842e110ed1395967f1354ee8865e1bf3a409c381da0391572d79e1ae41d89", "body_sha256": "75551329cb9be0350bb1965e5c58c7a5d3c3fd8d9131169405eed2a2d55d24ca", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P017", "submission_id": "10ukzpr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nrecently, my friends and i went to a restaurant for dinner, where i noticed there was a cute waiter that was serving us. i told my friends, not thinking much of it.\n\nthroughout the whole dinner, they proceeded to embarrass me about it, sometimes around the waiter, even asking to take a selfie with him. at the end of the dinner, while waiting for a friend to use the restroom, i noticed a friend of mine talking to the waiter 1v1, and i panicked, worried they'd embarrass me again but worse. i left (the bill was already paid for atp) and waited outside for them.\n\nthey all come out smiling and laughing, saying they told the waiter i thought he was cute, and they got his number. i felt beyond embarrassed now.\n\nthey put his number in my phone, and i said fuck it and sent a text. i wasn't expecting much to come out of this, so i was shocked to see him reply. we continued to talk throughout the night, even after my friends and i parted ways.\n\nthe next morning, i was happy, the waiter and i were having a good conversation the same morning.\n\nlater at lunch, my friend confessed that it wasnt the waiter that i was texting, it was my friend. my friend group was in on it, and even made a groupchat to laugh at me behind my back, leaking the messages and such.\n\ni was so mortified, they told me in front of most of our friend group (as i went to dinner with only 4 of them)\n\ni angrily left, sending a message to our discord server saying \"fuck you guys\" and went off on them.\n\nthey thought i was upset at being catfished, and while i am somewhat upset, i was mainly upset for being turned into a joke and laughed at behind my back by people who i called friends. 2 of them were my best friends.\n\nsome of them had said im overreacting, and some say im making it a bigger problem than it needs to be. my family says i should drop them, but idk what to do. some people say im right for being upset, and im not overreacting.\n\naita?", "prompt_sha256": "94327625acee7a7feaa187455ff7707b48d0497272eae40fb34d8c975b5f77d8", "body_sha256": "2296ff16cac8cef4dbbcfdfba6de523c2e27631f7b320cf1b68da69601f06c18", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P018", "submission_id": "1ehrxfr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo, the title might make me sound innocent enough, but let me give you the full context before you decide.\n\nA while back, my workplace was going through a particularly stressful period. Everyone was on edge, morale was low, and the tension was palpable. In an effort to lift everyone’s spirits, I came up with a light-hearted idea: a quiz to match each of our team members to a character from Winnie the Pooh. The idea was that everyone could anonymously vote on who they thought would be the best fit for each character—like who would be our Christopher Robin, who would be Winnie the Pooh, and so on.\n\nTo my relief, the plan worked like a charm. The quiz brought some much-needed levity to the team, and people seemed to genuinely enjoy it. I left the quiz open for a day to give everyone a chance to participate, and the next day, I published the results in our group chat. The feedback was overwhelmingly positive; it felt like everyone appreciated the fun distraction.\n\nRight after that, I took a week off work. During that time, I was actively job hunting and ended up securing a new position. When I returned to work, I handed in my notice.\n\nA few days later, I was unexpectedly called into a meeting with HR. To my surprise, I was informed that one of my colleagues was deeply upset about being voted as Eeyore. She had reportedly told HR that during a previous training session, we had discussed Winnie the Pooh characters as metaphors for mental health. Although I don’t recall having this conversation with her—especially since I didn’t attend many training sessions with her—I was now being accused of making a thoughtless, hurtful association.\n\nHR then told me that they were considering disciplinary action against me. However, because I had already resigned, they decided not to pursue it. But they made it clear that if I chose to retract my resignation, they would proceed with the disciplinary process.\n\nFast forward to my last day at the company. At 8:43 a.m., I posted a heartfelt goodbye message in our team Slack channel, expressing how much I’d miss everyone. I also mentioned that my 15-year-old stepchild had drawn a picture of Eeyore, which I included as a parting gift for my colleague. To me, it was a thoughtful gesture; the drawing was beautifully done, and I thought it would be a nice touch.\n\nBut less than an hour later, at 9:20 a.m., I was called into another meeting. Apparently, someone had filed a complaint about the Eeyore drawing, deeming it \"inappropriate and insensitive.\" The situation escalated quickly, and I was promptly escorted from the building.\n\nNow, Reddit, I’m left wondering: Was I really that out of line? AITA for sharing that drawing of Eeyore in my farewell message, or was this an overreaction on their part?\n", "prompt_sha256": "5c5a1e44b3190e02baa81634773b24b83c357eb6d36ab71d3457659060b55727", "body_sha256": "3d921510ee5b51a07b1b4bb123f767fc7b425603df0ddcdc8f780bbba7102036", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P019", "submission_id": "16cn4cy", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy GF (29F) and (33M) have been together for 3 years.  I bought a house a year into our relationship and she moved in with me about 9 months ago.  She has lived in apartments her entire life so she was extremely excited to have actually have space and a yard to call her own.  My house had an existing fenced-in garden area that the previous owners had let go into disrepair.  I am not a green thumb by any means, so I didn't do much with it either.\n\nWhen my GF moved in, she wanted to get the garden up and running again, so that was our Spring project.  We cleaned everything out, tilled the soil, and set up a few raised beds for veggies and herbs.  But my GF also wanted to get chickens.  I was hesitant to agree because I have a dog who I let out into the backyard and I don't know how he would react to chickens.  But instead of just saying \"no,\" I told her we need to look up ordinances and laws first and go from there.\n\nWithin hours she had found all the city ordinances and laws about backyard chickens and showed them all to me.  Apparently, we can have 3 chickens (no roosters) in their yard.  I told her she can have 2 chickens, but she has to pay for everything related to them and as far as I'm concerned, they are her pets to care for.  \n\nSo, she bought a coop with a fenced run area (that I had to assemble and set up heating), and we put it in the garden so that my dog could still have access to the yard without harassing the chickens.  She started letting the chickens out of the coop so that they could roam the yard (she calls it free-range), and after some introductions with my dog, they seemed to get along fine and my dog leaves them alone.  \n\nHowever, I didn't know how much chickens poop.  It's everywhere.  If you don't clean it up every day, it's everywhere.  With my dog, I go out there once or twice a week and pick up after him because he only goes in 1-2 spots.  But the chickens poop literally everywhere they go and you have to keep up on it much more often.  I complained to my GF about it multiple times and told her she needs to either keep them in the garden or clean up after them every day but she usually only does it when I pick up after my dog, or sometimes I just end up doing it.  \n\nShe won't keep them in the garden because they peck at the veggies and herbs.  She won't keep them in the coop because \"they've become accustomed to free-range and it makes them happier\" according to her.  \n\nWe had another fight about it the other day because I stepped in chicken poop while wearing sandals and it's gross.  I told her if the chickens are going to be in the yard, then she needs to pick up after them every single day.  She told me it's unreasonable to expect her to walk the entire yard everyday cleaning up poop when I only clean up after my dog twice a week.  \n\nI told her she either cleans up after them every day, keeps them in the coop or garden, or they're gone.  She thinks I'm being an AH about this and that I hate her pets and just want them gone.", "prompt_sha256": "24947d38b2293a46df2b7020e52bfe00e8fb2575497164905b4f960eb7d84aa0", "body_sha256": "17af7c002786469617433e2e4261d109ab77ed4d571c519c2bb02d14dc286409", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P020", "submission_id": "156vlun", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI was hanging out with some friends at the local park in the neighborhood and since I’m not so sporty, I decided to go to one of the friends’ house to chill with his younger sisters instead. While at their house, I had to take a shit pretty bad. Shitting in the girls’ bathroom felt a little wierd so I decided to go to the one next door in my friend’s room. \nWhile shitting, my friend comes home from the park not knowing that I was in his bathroom. I don’t remember exactly what was said, but he wasn’t okay with it. Once I was done, he had already left the house to go back to the park. I ended up going back too and when I did, it seemed like he was ignoring me. I sincerely apologized to him, but added that if our positions would be swapped, I would be fine with it. At one point, he told the other friends that all but one of us should go to one of their houses to chill there. Obviously offended, I apologized again, but he didn’t care. The other friends seemed to side with me a little, telling him to just let me come. I ended up just walking home to avoid further drama. \nI told my mom about the situation and she sided with me. A couple of days later, my parents went out with my friend’s parents for dinner. My mom went out of her way not to bring up the shituation, but when my friend’s mom brought it up saying that her son told her that he had asked me not to shit it his bathroom many times and that I was ignoring his requests, my mom “exploded.” \nWe would usually wave to each other in the halls or just say “hi,” but he was still ignoring me. I did catch him off guard a couple of times with a 😮 and managed to get a 😮 back from him, though.\nMy brother ended up talking to both of us and helped us get over it, and all is well now, but AITA for shitting in my friends bathroom?", "prompt_sha256": "04ce48af59bc5f3117739e63784ce4b92a31d66cdd1962a8b5183cc81e2c00b5", "body_sha256": "f1fa23fa949b97a2ec03938683aaceea7df6b8002731b963e66d44e24cf50563", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P021", "submission_id": "154yu91", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy mom (59), my dad (58) and my sister (28) are all JW and very devout. I(30F) was born into it and it’s all I knew growing up. The people in the congregation were my family. But, I was “expelled” when I was 19 and my family and everyone I knew turned their back on me. It was absolutely traumatic for me. After two years of begging and of “showing repentance” I was reinstated as JW. \n\nI was married by then to a “non believer” but my family started talking to me again. They (My mom, my dad and sister) showed lots of love to my son, sent him gifts and truly cared for him. After a few years away from them in a different state, I stopped congregating. My son was around 3 at the time and I started to open up to the idea of celebrating Halloween, birthdays, Christmas, etc. since it made my husband so happy. \n\nAs the years went by I realized my son would let my “dirty secret” slip and I would be either “expelled” and/or a complete disappointment to my family once again. I know, it’s past trauma and it’s unfair to put this on him but when he was around five I started to prep him before we would fly over to visit. I would tell him that my family didn’t like birthdays, Christmas, etc. so he cannot talk about that at all. To say “I don’t like that because God doesn’t like that” and he did. Through the years the lies have had to become a bit more elaborate and my son questions me as to why we don’t just go to the meetings like he does with my parents, I don’t know what to say or do. But I can’t imagine having my son go through the pain I went through to name just one of the million reason I will never go back. But, it’s a recurring nightmare in my life to lose my family again and for my son to lose them too. He loves them, and I do too however insane their beliefs are. \n\nI think about my son letting it slip that he had a birthday party and I start to sob thinking of the consequences of that. Of not seeing or speaking to my family again. My family is beginning to question why my son is not doing more in the congregation since he’s of age to do so…I make up something. I hate with all my heart that I’m teaching my son to lie, but the alternative is even more painful. My friends all turned on me after the “expulsion” so the only “friend” I have is my sister. I can’t tell her any of this obviously but I feel so alone in this. If you are an ex JW you could probably understand. But still AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "4ac8fdc00ea5952c807b0dc3423c613e6a964635a7b322797061797760036e31", "body_sha256": "47ce3af6d95958c8012b538e372a8fd71d0fae509fa04b07dda250cefc4bb173", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P022", "submission_id": "1eafp0i", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI 34f was away with my husband and 2 children we also went away with his brother and his family (wife and 2 kids). On the first full day of our stay we went swimming at had a great time! The second day I wore a bikini instead of a 1 piece bathing suit. My sister in law asked me to put my other bathing suit back on but it was still a little damp and I didn’t want to feel uncomfortable. She told me she was uncomfortable because I was “exposing myself to her husband and children” I told her bathing suits are very normal to see in public and that if she’s uncomfortable it’s her own issue. She has since gotten out husbands parents involved and the mother is saying it was fine that I wore the bathing suit and that she’s over reacting and the father thinks that I should have been more covered. ", "prompt_sha256": "e7802ccc6b73d608e8b09df12654caf7a198c1cabc87e9b6829712f58f468f00", "body_sha256": "0e988621ec6e6fc0a2b3133950e2938b36d940224f25576868d902c4c147ec61", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P023", "submission_id": "12eivy7", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nTL;DR\nMy husband throws his dirty clothes on the side of his bed instead of putting them in the hamper right next to his bed and expects me to pick up his dirty clothes and wash them. I’ve asked him several times to put his dirty clothes in the hamper if he wants me to wash them but will only do so once a month when it’s a bunch of clothes. \n\nWhole story\nMy husband (31M) and I (32F) were talking about this last night as I had a load of laundry going in the dryer when he got home from work. He thinks I’m wrong for not doing his laundry that he leaves on the floor. \n\nI started doing his laundry 3 years ago when we bought our house. Before that, we rented a place and did our own laundry. Because he wanted his clothes washed a certain way. But when we bought our house he asked if I could just wash his clothes with mine and I agreed. \n\nAt some point, he started to just wear his boxers to bed and would throw the rest of his clothes on the floor. When I noticed that he would just throw his clothes on the floor next to his side of the bed, I asked him to start putting his clothes in the laundry hamper in the master bathroom. He complained that it was too far and that he just takes his clothes off when’s he’s getting into bed. So I bought him a hamper and put it right next to his side of the bed. I thought problem solved. \n\nTurned out, I was wrong. He just throws his dirty clothes around the hamper instead of putting them in the hamper. I asked him to start putting his clothes in the hamper next to his side of our bed and he complained that it was too dark to see. But he doesn’t have a problem placing his phone on his night stand. I told him I won’t wash his clothes if they are on the floor. Only if they are in the hamper. So he started putting his clothes in the hamper for a couple of weeks. Then stopped. So I stopped washing the clothes that he leaves on the side of the bed(only washing what made it into the hamper). Then he got mad at me for not washing his clothes and asked me to start washing them again. I told him I would wash them if he put them in the hamper. I feel like this is a simple request. I’m doing him a favor by washing his clothes. Even if he doesn’t put them in the hamper right after he takes his clothes off, he could put them in the hamper in the morning when he wakes up. Or before he leaves our room each day. \n\nI do wash whatever he puts in the bathroom hamper. He doesn’t have a problem putting stuff in there but it’s usually only a few items. We both have full time jobs. I work remotely from home. I do the majority of the cooking and cleaning. Bills are split 60(him)/40(me). He makes more money and wants me to be able to save money for a rainy day so he agreed to pay more bills. No kids yet.", "prompt_sha256": "a6d143df8de37fb5dd50308f768e660e40504f744042969d289e0065c3420ac8", "body_sha256": "e32c9b8e88c96d837ee87cb9369ad76fee76a04569dd046c67b9fa9bc7ada6f5", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P024", "submission_id": "1i4658l", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy friend and I were hanging out at my place for almost the entire day yesterday. I told her about this amazing ice cream place at the mall and I'd treat her. At first she agreed and told me it's a great idea. Then she suddenly snapped and said that she can't eat ice cream because she's on this healthy diet, and she absolutely will not touch that stuff and it's wrong. I told her that she's not forced to eat it, that it was just a suggestion.\n\nIt just so happened that my work place (it's at the mall) needed my assistance and asked if I could come in for a few minutes to help them. (I live like 5-10 mins away from the mall so it's no problem). I told her we any ways have to go because my coworkers need help.  I told her we can hang at the mall for a bit if she's down. Any ways we were passing the ice cream place and I told her I'm grabbing some for my self and I asked her if she's sure that she does not want any. She said she's good and thanked me for offering.\n\nWe're browsing the mall and she tells me the ice cream actually looks really good if she could have a lick. I told her if she really wants it I'll get it for her no problem. But she said she just wants to try it from mine. I told her I'm not comfortable with that but the offer still stands about me getting her an ice cream. She got annoyed and said \"Why are you being such an AH about this I don't want a whole damn ice cream I just want a lick from yours\". I told her again I'm not comfortable with that.\n\nI'm just very weird when it comes to sharing food where spit could easily be exchanged, unless I'm very close with the person and I'm at a certain level of trust with them for example my mom or my brother. Like I could be good friends with some one but still not be comfortable sharing those types of food with them.\n\nMy friend and I are just good friends from college that is all.\n\nSo AITA? I mean I still offered to buy her an ice cream as an alternative.", "prompt_sha256": "7a93b718a79f94c99e57b4eaf7ec99effec376c969f3bf007d0ba53a81922e09", "body_sha256": "0e329a021a8a72c1cb24a35d4f641c5efbc178e27844a8277339795174508d45", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P025", "submission_id": "vca6z1", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy 21 yo daughter, part time engineering student, living at home, no job.  She’s a good kid, good student.  It’s tough getting her to do anything around the house to help out.  She always gives attitude when reminded to do her weekly chores or is asked to help out.  says she’s so busy with school, so stressed out, etc and huffs and puffs while doing what is asked of her.  She hasn’t gotten job since high school because she is so busy with school ( mind you, she only had three classes this semester).    But she’s recently engaged to a wonderful young man and she ALWAYS has time for him, his family or her church activities.   And fiancé is at our house every day.  If she’s home, he’s here.    I cook most nights of the week, (and I despise cooking).    She and fiancé stay in her room and come out to eat and then back to the room.   No help with dishes or cooking or anything.   So recently I said to her, hey, at least pitch in every now and then.   And, maybe switch it up, you know sometimes eat at his parents house.   Because with a wedding this year, two kids in college, plus my youngest rodeos (which is hella expensive), money is a little tight and I’m not keen on adding an extra mouth to feed every day.  My husband thinks I’m the AH for saying something about the fiancé eating here every day.    And I do feel like an AH.   What do y’all think, AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "12316142a4dd754bb73c649dd202fe31094080da9f11c12eb31b395529adf9a7", "body_sha256": "865a4b40f731d98f33397934f235d6b9777b4ff8774f71ec59e3cb2c4d0e255f", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P026", "submission_id": "y68ihz", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo my MIL is going downhill fast. She's been in ill for several years now but due to a heart attack they've changed her medication so now her BP has sky rocketed and she's had several falls.\n\nMy husband promised his dying father that he would look after his mum. He felt better placed to do this as at the time he was single and his sister had teenage children.\n\nNow he is married, and we have 4 small children. \n\nHis sister has been down this weekend (lived 4 hours away) and would not hear of MIL may need in the not to distant future to go into a home/assisted living because my husband had promised their father, and that I need to get back in lane because I'm not really part of the family (that's a whole other story) and what difference does it make if for the time being my husband leaves me with the children and moves in with his mum to keep her out of a home. Because he promised his dad.\n\nI tried to point out that SIL knows how to play my husband...and will continue to use a promise he made as a young single man to enforce her will on him...she's not offering any help. They were here this weekend, and so husband came home for the first time in a month to spend the night with me and the children. She didn't do anything to help his mum up to bed and got grumpy when MIL woke her at 11am to help her down so she could get herself a drink and food. She didn't want to call my husband because she's very aware that he's spent very little time with the children or me and wanted us to enjoy it.\n\nShe was considering moving into a home, but SIL told her not to allow my husband's selfishness to force her to do something she doesn't want to do.\n\nWhenever husband starts arguing with her she brings up his promise to his dad.", "prompt_sha256": "b1f9cb1178b5dd6e7cf11deed10ebf48c48f6bb0bd212b7c636b11685923d369", "body_sha256": "bd3dd25723a5fd293798db3257f7a02d4cf0044dabe881d30e5e0faf1d96541e", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P027", "submission_id": "uarufp", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHello people, I(13M) am fuming right now.... I wanted to vent somewhere and also find out if I did anything wrong, so here we go.\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nMy cousins(12F, 13M) are.....BEING SPOILED BY MY GRANDMA(I forgot her age). Hear me out, my aunt is a person who literally traps them in the house, no YouTube no tv no video games and no phone, and my parents are literally the opposite, i got a phone and a Nintendo switch(important l8r) when i turned 13. The only restriction i have is no technology that isn't tv after 9 30 pm, my cousins WHINE every time I come over or they come over they just whine to my grandma that I have it better, i mean i agree but it sometimes gets annoying and i do try and make them feel better, i give them my switch for a couple hour, i let them play on my PC etc.\n\nIn September 2021, I had my 13 birthday, after years of begging, my parents got me a Nintendo switch with smash bros and a mobile phone. If i saw someone who got that i would be sad that i dont have it myself but wouldn't **complain to my grandma that i dont have that and demand that i get one.** YES they did that. I was angry but let it go. And here it starts, the blackmail drama...\n\nThere are a lot of other stories of my cousins gaslighting my grandma with lies that i was bragging and showing off in many stuff. One example is literally last week when my mom and i decided to go on a ice cream shopping spree, we bought a bunch of ice cream\\` for the summer and they complained to my grandma and she literally took 3/4 of the ice creams and gave them to my cousins...Like WHAT!!!!\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nAnd here is the part where i snapped,\n\nYesterday, i got Minecraft dungeons for my switch and mentioned it to my cousins and the drama begins again, they go to my grandma but this time it changes, they apparently demand that they should get MY switch and i was ungrateful. My grandma F\\*\\*KING SAID OK!!!!. Infront of my eyes she took the switch, the dock and all my games and accessories. (PS: my parents were in the kitchen while all this happened)Here is the convo that ensued.\n\nMe-me\n\nGM-Grandma\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nMe - \"Woah what are you doing!!\"\n\nGM - \"I'm giving your game thingy to your cousins...they deserve it more than you\"\n\nMe - \"WHAT!!! HOW DO I NOT DESERVE IT!!\"\n\nGM - \"You always show off about this thing and they always get sad when they come here\"\n\nMe - \" First of all, i don't quote unquote show off my stuff and I do let them play on it whenever we meet...apparently they didn't tell that. Second of all, MY DAD WORKED HIS ASS OF TO BUY ME THIS AND WHY WOULD I GIVE IT TO SOMEONE WHO DOSENT EVEN LET ME TOUCH A BOARDGAMEAT THEIR HOUSE!!!!\"\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nBoom. My grandma and cousins left in a huff, in my anger i forgot to check if they took the switch and they took it, don't worry i grabbed it before they could leave the house.\n\nMy aunt and parents are on my side but do think that i was rude. So, internet AITA for blowing up on my grandma?", "prompt_sha256": "d30b2df2b55dec655386625329a90b65b72d947d34cdaeb718c47173b359c378", "body_sha256": "de14aea813c13a3e09d9d43d282ac0af2378e87c56e29ab689e1bf6ca5035d44", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P028", "submission_id": "zvit1x", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHello so my cousin (19F) and I (20F) planned on coming  to my grandma’s house together, since we both live in different cities and haven’t seen each other in a while. I arrived on a Thursday and she came on a Wednesday everything was normal and fine. We decided to go to a bar (it’s legal to drink where I’m at) and had a few drinks with her friend and her friend’s cousin. We were listening to music laughing and just generally having a nice time.  After a while we all got pretty drunk and she started talking to us about a guy that she’s been dealing with and how much he’s hurt her feelings because of his general lack of interest in a relationship, this then escalated to her telling us that she was pregnant and had taken a test the day prior. We all freaked out since she’s so young but we were willing to be there for her in every way possible, even though my cousin and I aren’t particularly the closest.\n\nThe next day after we sobered up a bit we went to my grandmas house finally, and all throughout the time we were there all she did was break down in tears because she claimed to be so frustrated and upset, she essentially spent the whole christmas upset and I consoled her throughout it all, she would complain about how pregnancy is bloating her and making her emotional and crying about having to have an abortion to not disappoint her parents. She also asked me to wear her uncomfortable shoes for her, since shes pregnant and everything hurts and I obliged. She also ended up telling the guy she was pregnant and he was worried and frantic because she was ignoring him and he couldn’t get ahold on her. On Christmas day she kept breaking down tears talking about how hard it’s been for her and I of course empathized and we also built a little bit of a bond.\n\nSo on Sunday night I ask her “how far along do you think you are?” And she answers with “I don’t know” and I tell her she should try her hardest to find out as soon as possible. She then starts freaking out and getting anxious since the guy was frantically texting her and I tell her she should just answer and work it out with the father. She then turns to me and says “there’s nothing to work out, because this is a prank. I lied and took it too far”. I at first didn’t believe her since she lied so well and I confronted her and asked her how could she ever do something like that? She answered with “Don’t be so dramatic it was just a prank.” But I honestly after this can’t bring myself to speak to such a manipulative person because her ability to so casually lie, fabricate tears and all that just for attention is scary and I never plan on speaking to her again. She claimed I was being cold and if I wanna stay mad and be cruel that’s fine and she wont chase after me, so AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "ae18458d3faf31431ef387a5fda59acd721a2e1748630ad3fc0d4f023ff69567", "body_sha256": "804e95b996371c1beeb1bff1579178a6b3cbde217b3e869663fb099a80611796", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P029", "submission_id": "var92b", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (30m) have had a horrible last year. \nEnd of last year my father, who lived with me, passed away. And soon after I found out my mother was sick. \n\nTo help my mom(66F) and get away from everything that was going on, I packed up my wife and kids and moved them back home across the country. \n\nMy older brother(48m) was staying with her at the time and was stealing money from her, not taking her to appointments, pawning her stuff, ect. And I found once I moved in that he was also on Meth(this news came out after he stole my sons(9m) bike). So I chased him off to keep him away from our mother and definitely my kids. After a few weeks my mom broke down and moved him back in with promises he would stop doing drugs and get a job. \n\nI began taking my mom to appointments as soon as I got here, and turns out she has stage 4 lung cancer. \n\nShe quit working and I began paying most of the bills, and my wife and I began doing everything for her from going to store, helping her shower, making her food, and giving her meds. Since she can no longer even stand out of bed for longer than a few minutes without getting out of breath. \n\nEvery month she ask me to pay more and more of the bills because she can’t afford them, but she is paying for my brothers car payment, insurance, and giving him money. \n\nLast week I had my last straw with my brother, I found a baggy in drive way with drug residue and he asked if I would give him money or buy a stolen tablet from him so that he could get away from the house, because he had drugs in the car. \n\nI told my mom I can’t have someone like this around my kids and if she was going to let him stay, we would be leaving… she told me “okay I guess you are leaving” \n\nYesterday I got approved for a rental and sign papers this week and get keys. Knowing he does nothing for her I feel almost like I am leaving her to die. And my other siblings, aunts, and uncle are all telling me I am wrong to leave. (All the same people who lived within 20 minutes of her and never took her to appointments or helped her, and asked me to move 2500 miles back home to do it)\n\nBut with everything.. AITA for really leaving and putting my family first?", "prompt_sha256": "90f167163fe01f85368c26280c363db8b2ae8b6c76b1e6e6fa017ab50f964d79", "body_sha256": "3f1fd74ae01ea30094e73b0687f95fe54c523d188d43c636bdbe7630beee5087", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P030", "submission_id": "1bcwtqo", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy sister who recently moved overseas for work with her family recently got very angry when my dad booked a flight to visit them in a few months without telling her until AFTER he had already made the booking. She said it was very rude and disrespectful to do that, especially when she had previously told our family not to book flights to visit her without giving her the heads up first. This was as recently as a couple of months ago when I had also made a booking for my own family to fly over to visit on our holiday without telling her until after we had made our plans and booked our flights.  \nI think she is just being difficult, and she should just live in the moment, and I think it’s a nice surprise to just make our plans and tell her, but she says it’s rude and disrespectful and assumes that she will now need to organise her own plans with work and her own holiday leave around us when we visit.\n\nThere was also an incident in the past where she and her husband booked a flight to visit our family, but we had forgotten about it and booked a trip for my family and our parents and so there ended up being no family in town for her to visit when her flight was already booked.  \nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "28cdce09c9cc910b91ab7bac33140d835961894783dfb354a3792f965e751c20", "body_sha256": "ea039d3c50791e98293992599566c1a356a1ffe3732cca7ee468bd88bdfba0ff", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P031", "submission_id": "u2ime0", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (26,F) sister (24,F, Mandie) recently did something to me that not only hurt me, but also enraged me. \n\nWe were both looking for jobs at the same time. I helped my sister write her resume (she did not help me with mine). I was so happy for her when she moved to the next round for one of her top choices. They asked her to send a sample of a PowerPoint she did, but she did not have one. \n\nI modified a PowerPoint I did in my previous job for her to send to them. When they moved her to the next round, they asked for a portfolio on a PowerPoint. I didn't help as much with this one, however I did embed links for her and provided detailed feedback anytime she asked (most of which she used).\n\nA week after she got a job offer, I was notified that I was moving to the third round (a group call) for my first choice. I asked my sister to send me the the portfolio she made because I wanted to use a similar format for my portfolio (which I planned to send to the group during / after my interview).\n\nAt first, my sister said she would send it to me but seemed in no rush to help. I asked her again later that day, and once again the following morning. The third time I asked her, she freaked out on me and said \"why does everyone in the house rely on me to do everything\". She didn't end up sending me the document. \n\nFlash forward to a few days later. My sister is stating her new job. She's already asked me for help with her WHIMIS training, and I politely declined. Today she was panicking because she needs to fill out TD1 by the end of tomorrow, otherwise she doesn't get paid for another three weeks.\n\n I know where my mom keeps those documents, and how to fill out the form. My sister asked me for help because she knows I've done this for my last job. I was making dinner, so I said \"no, because everyone in the house relies on me to do everything\". \n\nMy sister started crying and said that \"she'd remember this\". She doesn't even realize that I was saying the exact thing she said to me when I asked her for help. \n\nAm I an asshole for literally not giving a shit that she won't be paid for another three weeks. I don't care if she fails her WHIMIS training (I'm sure she won't, but IDC). \n\nAlso, am I an asshole if I don't explain to her why I'm doing this to her? Part of what pisses me off is how self-absorbed she is and, given her history, I don't think she'll think she did anything wrong no matter how hurt I am. \n\n**TL;DR** I went above and beyond to help my sister write her resume, and get a job by letting her pass my work as her own. When I needed help, she didn't help me and even yelled at me.. all I asked her for was to send a file. Now she's starting her job, I am not helping her with basic things (i.e. filling her TD1 so she can get paid this week). She freaked out on me for not helping, not noticing it was the same thing she said t me when she refused to help. I don't even intend on explaining why I won't help her (unless she asks).", "prompt_sha256": "981772509a78c592cd582e11a735b0bc09393d90eef7feca9f7ca824c49513f2", "body_sha256": "4f97a60d8b098a117224c2214a09840cd4d662bd87dc089ec3931196964a9ce4", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P032", "submission_id": "my9quq", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (32m) have supported my wife (32f) and daughter since our daughter was born. Recently my wife got a job and gets paid pretty well, not as much as me, but pretty well. \n\nI only ask her to pay for childcare, I pay the rest (both cars, insurance, cellphones, internet, rent, utilities, groceries). She constantly tells me that she only has so much money in her account and rarely pays for stuff when we go do things. She also hides her account balance from me, while having full access to my account which is a joint account. \n\nWe constantly bicker about her lack of willingness to pay for stuff because she \"doesn't have money.\" She will not hesitate to use my money for stuff because she says I have all the money. \n\nToday she said she only had a few dollars to get some food on the way home. She asked me if I wanted some food and I said well it sounds like you don't have enough money. Her response was that she will just use my card to pay for the food. I once again get aggravated that she will not ever use her money for us, but doesn't hesitate to use mine. \n\nAITA for being aggravated at my wife for hoarding her money while freely using mine, while I pay for the majority of the bills?", "prompt_sha256": "87ef10d52e13eb395ca08678ebbd8b2695b2d9fb91d8b7c217a7a77a2fcd20b0", "body_sha256": "8d985fb28612eb2bcabf4e36d66e9f92f277e4684c469e3ff68f8167740b106b", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P033", "submission_id": "euttsz", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI am 17f and I had a job as a camp counselor last summer. It was horrible.\n\nThe pay was hourly but we all worked way more hours than we are allowed to report on our time sheets. Minors are only allowed to work 48 hours a week but there is really no time off at camp. The day starts at 7 am and ends at 10 pm. Not to mention if kids wake up in the middle of the night, or pee their beds, then more time. So 15 hour workdays, 7 days a week. 105 hours a week. We're only allowed to report 48 a week, which means only getting paid for 48 a week. \n\nThere is no cell service or access to landlines for us, no internet access, no transportation except cars on or off the camp which is deep in the woods. None of us 16 or 17 year olds had cars. I feel like more people would quit on the spot if they had a way to leave. \n\nSo, onto the drama. Two months into the summer, the camp was having a staffing problem. They'd fired one guy. That guy's three best friends quit on the spot with him. Two international counselors quit soon after. \n\nI was working at the arts and crafts shed, along with Tom who's 17. We're good friends and I kinda have a crush on him.\n\nOne of the girls in our group was the camp owner's daughter, who is really really spoiled, she's used to getting everything she wants if she says \"but Susan's my mom!\"\n\nShe wanted more craft supplies, and I said no, every child only gets three because we need enough for everyone. She started a screaming crying fit going \"But I want them! My mom's Susan, you have to give me them! you have to!\" It was silly but it was my last straw, and I was like \"Actually I don't have to do anything.\" She goes \"Yes you have to, Susan's your boss\"\n\nAnd I go \"Not anymore.\" I went to leave and Tom followed me, he said he was done here too. We ran into another counselor with a radio on the path and said they should radio the office to send someone else to the crafts shed, we were quitting.\n\nWe packed our duffles and walked away, it took us almost four hours to walk the dirt road out of camp and to the nearest small town, where we went into the dollar store and asked to use a phone because we had no cell reception. His parents were only two hours away so they came to get us that night.\n\nThings apparently got crazy behind us. The counselor we'd told about quitting didn't know who we were so nobody knew who had quit for a while. The camp director was furious at us for having left the children alone, but also furious that we, two minors, had walked off with no ride and no communication with parents. I guess we were in a weird place where we were employed and responsible for children while also legally being children they were responsible for...\n\nAITA for quitting and walking out?", "prompt_sha256": "5d71542394ee03479c9a33dbd3a2d5fe1dda0737329a53f541a47e5f485e6d3d", "body_sha256": "8109a3dd120d23cd7c6a831dd494c6d7a32041c098dda7fedcf361db8e88751e", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P034", "submission_id": "gsr7bf", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo recently I bought a map making software for my dnd sessions and I really like it, I found out that the app was basically solely made by a dude and I'm glad to support his hard work via paying for the software, which I find not to be overpriced.\n\nHowever, since there is no login to the app or any sort of anti piracy measure to it, you can pretty much zip the file and share it with friends. I was told this by one of my friends / players in my campaign and he asked if I could send it to him for his own campaign.\n\nKeep in mind, before I had this, I used free software available online, and I indicated that friend to using that one if he can't get the paid one.\nHe got mad about it and still insists on me giving the software for free to him.\n\nI don't really intend in doing it, not because I had to pay for it, but because I don't really support the kind of attitude of \"why should it bother you to give it to me\" that people tend to have on these situations. \n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e0dbf063b104e418dd30ff42a5e17c70ae1d1796e71ac77c554ac8e440c855ce", "body_sha256": "1c2766cde549360bbbe678a9eeeaecdca7bca2dc8b718318d96d22d9048c4fbc", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P035", "submission_id": "ly3002", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n***ETA: Thank you to those who have given their judgment &amp; your kind words. Just to clear some assumptions/ questions that were asked:***\n\n1. ***Why the hard deadline? I teach in a campus that answers to a parent campus (if that makes sense). The deadline was not of my doing &amp; its implemented throughout the entire university &amp; its courses. I have been flexible to students to approach me personally cause I know shit happens &amp; its occasionally unavoidable.*** \n2. ***Why the proof? Again, the policy is not of my own doing but had the student said that were not comfortable sharing proof, I would have thought of an alternative. But because he had escalated the matter before we could come to a satisfactory conclusion, it was put into his records.***\n3. ***Why the high weightage? Again, this is a campus-wide policy that was implemented by the higher ups. I'm a professor but not the HoD so I answer to my superior, who then answers to their boss and so forth. If I could, I would have implemented the staggered, progressive way as suggested by a commentor. I have recommended it before but the higher ups didn't like it.***\n4. ***I didn't know he was on academic probation. Again, had I known, I would have thought of an alternative. And had he clarified why I had given the other student an extension (they provided the proof required by the uni within 24 hours), I would have gladly explained.***\n5. ***Was there an alternate contact? Yes. In the course outline, the online materials, etc the name &amp; contact of the other professor was provided in case I cannot be reached.*** \n6. ***Why was I dragged into that meeting? My superior didn't tell the Dean, of which they (my superior) later apologised.*** \n7. ***I did write my superior a recommendation that he still be able to submit the assignment at a later date. My superior told me that because he was on academic probation, there would be another meeting to decide but they would take my suggestion into account.***\n\nHappened a month ago but I still feel guilty over it. I'm a professor &amp; my students had an assignment due on the week I was on bereavement leave. I informed my students of this, and let them know that I would be answering emails/ requests late, so it was better to inform the other professor in charge of the unit. This assignment was given at the beginning of the semester &amp; they were informed that no deadline extension would be provided unless there was an emergency (with proof) or requested in advance cause it was the school's policy.\n\nOne of student's grandmother passed the day the assignment was due, so she emailed me &amp; CCed the other lecturer. I happened to see the email in time, &amp; I made a note in the system of her case &amp; the deadline was extended with subsequent action pending the submission of proof.\n\nA day after the deadline, another student emailed me (only) saying that he couldn't submit his assignment due to personal reasons &amp; asked for a backdated extension. I didn't see the email until a couple of days later. Because of the delay, he received an automatic fail. I emailed him back explaining what had happened but if he could provide proof of the emergency I may be able to find a solution where he won't be failed (but won't be given high marks). He sent a really nasty reply &amp; CCed the dean &amp; my superior (the other lecturer in charge of the unit). I was dragged into an online meeting to sort this issue (while on my bereavement leave).\n\nHe called me a shitty professor because I was on leave the week the assignment was due &amp; I was playing favourites cause I gave an extension to his classmate but not him &amp; didn't answer his email on time. He also said that I had no right to ask for proof because it was personal. I interrupted him to tell him off, saying that I honestly don't give a shit about what excuses he has because I have proof that he acknowledged my emails. I also said that I'm sorry that my brother's death inconvenienced him but that it was his responsibility to keep track of dates &amp; understand that certain things were out of my control because it's the school's policy, not mine. I also reminded him that I did say that I would try to not fail him but I couldn't do that if I didn't have proof. I admit I was not as polite as I normally would be, &amp; I was visibly upset by the time the Dean cut in.\n\nThe Dean apologised to me first because he had no clue I was on bereavement leave (apparently my superior didn't tell him for whatever reason). He then said I could excuse myself from the meeting cause he would settle this matter with my superior. I left the meeting &amp; I found out later that the student was already on academic probation &amp; would possibly be expelled cause he failed my unit (assignment was 60% of overall grade). He also came from a troubled background, which explained the personal reasons.\n\nI really do care for my students, &amp; knowing I may have contributed to him being expelled from the university does not sit well with me.", "prompt_sha256": "ae15a2068e3289a6c3bae090ac7be66018b2adbd16e29f7fad25d879e29305d8", "body_sha256": "30718b48f7ab5df3887d4822980334c2c6c26520a93ecaec8a0ab37322d1a5a2", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P036", "submission_id": "g2hyoe", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI’m in a group chat with 8 other people. We all go to the same grad school. John said: “Hi everyone. I received a diagnosis.” He never even announced he was sick or seeing a doctor, at least to me, so I was afraid that he had cancer or something similarly serious.  Another friend responded: “Oh no, is everything okay?”  After a two-hour long pause, John said, “I will be okay...now. I have been diagnosed with ADHD.”\n\nAs a person with ADHD, this struck me as obviously being much less serious than a terminal diagnosis, and not worth the drama. I said, “Man, I thought you were dying or something, that was really dramatic!” He didn’t respond to me and the conversation moved on. A mutual friend of me and John messaged me and told me that John was very offended by what I said. John thinks that I was minimizing his very serious diagnosis, a diagnosis he sees as a revelation and the reason he’s always struggled to succeed in work/school.  Since this was told to me in a covert way, I didn’t see a space to apologize or explain myself.  I don’t even know what I would say...That I still think that saying “I received a diagnosis” in a group chat and announcing an ADHD diagnosis is overdramatic?\n\nAm I being an asshole here?", "prompt_sha256": "c84df1a2fa5589c3a2d348d13547791dc96e6d2d650b8e4e4c7308a8d5a030f1", "body_sha256": "298faf536d09ffa4a1a5c44493f74b06401349ff204214a31adbe5aeab0a64d8", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P037", "submission_id": "q1cbjr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nA group of my girlfriends and I have been planning a wine-tasting trip for a couple months. We rented a shuttle bus for the day to drive us around to a few different vineyards   We all have kids so we had to plan it out in advance so we could all make arrangements for childcare.  My husband was going to stay home with our 3 girls (9, 6, &amp; 3) for the day.  This is one of the first times I've been able to see these friends like this in the last 2 years so I was really looking forward to it.\n\nThe night before the trip, my husband is in the bathroom all night.  He must have eaten something that disagreed with him and I don't think he got much sleep at all.  The next morning I got up and started to get myself ready and he was still in bed.  I woke him up to remind him that I was leaving and that he needed to get up to take care of the girls.  He just moaned at me and asked me if I was seriously still going.\n\nI told him of course I'm going.  I've been looking forward to this for weeks.  He told me he got no sleep and still doesn't feel good and just needs some rest.  I told him he's just going to need to suck it up because I'm not staying home.  I'm finally able to convince him to at least get out of bed because the girls are awake and need supervision.  When I left he was laying on the couch.\n\nThe trip with my friends was great and exactly the kind of break I needed.  We laughed and had some good wine and danced like idiots.  It was perfect.  \n\nWhen I got home the place was a mess.  There were toys and dolls everywhere.  My two youngest girls didn't have clothes on.  The kitchen was a disaster with food and dirty dishes all over.  And of course, my husband was still on the couch.  \n\nI asked him what the hell he did all day since the place was a disaster.  He said he still felt like crap and he just let the girls run wild since he didn't have the energy to chase them.  He said the girls are happy and fed, no one got hurt, and I got to go drink wine all day with my friends, so how about I cut him a little slack.\n\nI told him that this was beyond even my lowest expectations for him.  He said he didn't have the energy to fight about it and he was going to bed.  I asked him if he was going to help clean any of this up and he told me if I wanted it clean right now I was going to have to do it, otherwise it's going to stay the way it is until morning when he hopefully feels better. \n\nI'm kind of a neat freak so of course I anger-cleaned after the girls went to bed.  The next morning I told my husband how disappointed I was with him and he got pissed at me.  He said I was the one who left to go drink all day, knowing he didn't feel good. He said I should just be happy that I was still able to go out with friends given how crappy he felt the day before.  \n\nI told him it wasn't my fault he got sick and that I wasn't going to pat him on the back for doing the absolute bare minimum of watching our kids.", "prompt_sha256": "6ea5a2e0d3bb48df4fef07d25ed2ee9ccb0f0f3492839078d3280ceccd6fabdb", "body_sha256": "bab7e956333b63612f70f291d1101a47fea9c4d440900994d7c267f184f1b808", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P038", "submission_id": "inu97u", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy late wife passed away three years ago, I been married with my current wife for 6 months now.\nMy son (15) disrespects my wife and would always hurt her with his words.\n\nI tried to get him to get used to his new life but he always says he can't wait to leave.\n\nMy son has always wanted to go to college, he's aiming to go study at his favorite which is out of the state.\nHe wants to be a doctor it's his dream, his mom passed away from cancer and he said he wanted to be a doctor, do researches to help people with this type of diesease, I thought that this shows the good side of him and how emapathatic he can be, I just don t get why he doesn't get along with his stepmom, she's always nice to him, her feelings were hurt when he yelled at her for cleaning up his room this morning.\n\nI told him that if he doesn't start treating my wife with respect then I won't save up any money for his college and will just send him to a tuition-free community college.\n\nHe got mad at me, told me I was trying to buy him with my money, and that I was being a horrible daf, he brought up his friends and how lucky they were to have good dads, I cut the conversation and told him to go to his room, he started crying and said that I care about what my wife wants more than him.\n\nI was just trying to give him consequences for his behavior but it just got worse, he doesn't want to talk to me anymore.", "prompt_sha256": "104928af2a0a8a2be05d7b5683f616a51fe82248b46591545402a3987b38ecc3", "body_sha256": "2f5ebbaf990f1bb7b17ae6473effad876c3f615945183dbe28c6482044975668", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P039", "submission_id": "1czsk5w", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI’m 16M and I have been homeschooled by my father for pretty much my entire life, my mom died when I was 5 and then my dad took me out of school and started to homeschool me. \n\nWhen I was younger I enjoyed homeschool a lot and I remember loving that I got to spend so much time with my dad. But I never really had any friends, I did go to Scouts but that was just for 1 hour a week and dad never lets anyone come over to our house or lets me go out with friends. So most of my friends are from Reddit and discord. \n\nI’ve approached my dad about me joining back with normal school but he doesn’t want me to. But I really want to, so I applied (Idk if that’s the right word) for the college in our town in secret and I was just going to go with the “ask for forgiveness, not permission” route with my dad and hope things worked out. \n\nBecause I didn’t want my dad to find out my friend I made on discord told me to put down my address as his address (we live in the same town) so if they send any post my dad won’t see that I’ve applied. They sent out all these forms that need to be signed by my dad, but obviously he won’t sign them. My friend said that he will sign them pretending to be my dad for me. \n\nThough I want to go, I’m starting to feel nervous about the whole thing. I worried about if my dad goes mad at me for signing up. My dad will definitely be mad at me for doing it and he will be super mad if he knows I’ve got someone to fake sign the forms for him. \n\nMy friend is encouraging me to do it anyway, but now I’m getting second thoughts and will just probably not do it because I’m worried about how my dad is going to react. I think probably this was all a stupid idea anyway because I don’t even know how I would get to college everyday. \n\nBut on the other hand I really want to be normal and I don’t feel normal being homeschooled and stuck here all the time and my friend says if I do go we can finally meet up in person. He doesn’t go there but he said he can meet me up after the day or something.  So that makes me want to go it. \n\nWIBTA?", "prompt_sha256": "08c30a5a0811a679f0ef415bf70e24da92c0468d623face7e03b1645a11cd32d", "body_sha256": "54e66ab6f9ae18c9f02f30c4c6a77f7f03bcb96967dfd5b364847f53de07c28a", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P040", "submission_id": "1k4a6ob", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nUgh. This is so stupid but I'm still mad about it.\n\nYesterday my girlfriend (32F) and I (35F) threw a little combination Easter-4/20 get-together for some friends in a large public park that included, as one element, an Easter egg hunt. This is a big local park where people often do small private egg hunts for their families and friends, so the idea isn't totally out there. We bought around 100 plastic eggs, stuffed each one with 2-3 pieces of candy, and hid them within a smallish area of the park about 20 minutes before everyone else was due to arrive. We figured because the weather was nice, we'd probably lose a few eggs due to kids walking by and stumbling on easy-to-find ones, but we bought enough that we could absorb some marginal losses. Some were pretty visible, others psychotically well-hidden, most were pretty much in the middle - you'd have to really be looking to spot them walking by.\n\nWhile we were waiting for all of our friends to arrive, we noticed three kids running around the area where we'd hidden them, and they all had their arms FULL of eggs. Like 15-20 apiece easily. Their mom was sort of trailing behind, not paying attention, and on the phone. It got to a point where we finally got her attention and she literally went, \"Is it okay if they take these?\" My GF and I were both dumbfounded. Because, again, we figured we'd lose a few eggs to kids who grabbed one or two. But this was EGREGIOUS. They had easily 50 between them. There were 15 people coming. Yes, they were all adults, but adults also like to have silly fun too!\n\nSo we basically told her, uh, no? Please put them back? Her response was some version of \"They're just kids! It's a kids' holiday!\" I asked her if she usually lets her kids take candy from strangers off the ground in public parks, and said something along the lines of, \"Weird parenting choice, but okay,\" and she got huffy and told the kids they were leaving and to put them back. The kids threw some of the eggs on the ground but still left with probably 40 eggs in total. Again, that's... 80-120 pieces of candy that we bought. For our friends. And ourselves. Not for random children who didn't even bother to ask before taking it. (If they'd asked, we probably would've said sure, within reason! 2-3 apiece! NOT LITERALLY HALF OF THEM.)\n\nAlso, as they were leaving my girlfriend called after them, \"Good luck finding the ones filled with fentanyl,\" which was very funny, but I don't think they heard.\n\nAnyway, now I feel like an AH for calling her a bad parent in front of her kids and for ruining their fun, but I also have a real tendency to feel insanely guilty any time I stand up for myself (blame my own mom's stellar parenting for that!), so I just wanted a temperature check. This was objectively insane behavior, right? Or am I the asshole?", "prompt_sha256": "5888fea9632cf6d0594ef3232581ed5a0183d95ac9ed0d532673e141fb4c0bb6", "body_sha256": "e36ec1e6b56b7a60e098455fde6e7205edd79bd0fe0d897ba753486798a42779", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P041", "submission_id": "k7uuwb", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nOkay so, me and my fiancée hosted Thanksgiving this year. We were safe, the only people we had over were my older brother and his family and my older sister and her kids. We all quarantined for 14 days before the day they drive over to my city. My bother and his wife have a 4 year old girl and an 8 year old boy. My sister has a 7 year old boy and a 2 year old girl.\n\nI don’t know this when it happened but my brother and sister made plans to let their kids bring their bikes so they could play when we weren’t all together as a family. One of the days they were here, my brother and his wife decided to drive around to explore and wanted me and our sister to watch the kids. I love my nieces and nephews so of course I took care of them. \n\nThe boys got kinda restless and wanted to go outside to play, my sister told me about their bikes and I went to unload them and saw that my bother’s son’s bike had training wheels. I asked him why and he said he couldn’t ride the bike normally. I wasn’t going to do anything about it but I eventually could tell he was jealous that his cousin didn’t need training wheels. So I taught him how to ride the bike without training wheels. It took a while but he got the hang of it and was a pro by the evening.\n\nThe rest of the visit went great and they left. I’m guessing this week my brothers kids are out of school for the holidays so he’s playing more outside. I got a call from my brother and he was livid. He asked if I taught my nephew how to ride without training wheels. I told him yeah, I showed him how to ride the bike. My brother lost his fucking mind. He told me that I should’ve never done that and called me a bunch of horrible names. \n\nI asked why he knew his son still needed training wheels at 8, he said that he just got him the bike and was gonna teach him over the Christmas break. I told him that he should’ve told me that, he said that he didn’t think he’d need to tell me to not teach his only son how to ride a bike. We argued back and forth and he hung up on me.\n\nI kinda feel like shit, but I didn’t know I should’ve taught him.\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "335f3a031a6c3458dae039beded3e0823512f0b5cf3fcab57c3a2f0ebdaf0f62", "body_sha256": "ff544f2df46c41f620f9c246acf7392a46e687997015b1114f1cbd0bd111fcfe", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P042", "submission_id": "1hc29d8", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nLoooong time lurker, so here to figure out if I'm wrong here.\n\nMy (36F) boyfriend (32M) of two years is a bit on the irresponsible and immature side. We had VERY different upbringings (he is upper middle class and lived at home until moving in with me last year, while I had a very rough childhood and moved out 2 weeks after turning 18) so he wasn't really forced to grow up as fast as I was. This comes out in different ways, but the most recent way is his car. \n\nHis car broke down 5 months ago. It needs a fairly simple part, but he has just let it sit for the past 5 months. We use my car for everything, which, yes irks me and I have told him I don't like him taking my car all day or that we use it all the time, but he usually reverts to he doesn't have the money to fix his. \n\nWe do have a large income gap, he makes about 30k to my 150k so I also pay for everything. His only expenses are his cell phone and car insurance. I pay rent, utilities, food, internet, all the household expenses. \n\nHis job is also intermittent (he is crew in the entertainment industry). He has a job coming up that will require him to be out of town for 3 days. I've told him he is not taking my car and leaving me stranded for 3 days. Do I have anywhere super important to go? Not really, but its my car. I paid for it. I would like to use it when I want. He get very sad looking and apologized that he doesn't make very much money which made me feel horrible. \n\nBut the thing is, the part needed to fix his car is $200 and he can put it in himself. He recently bought $170 headphones, two video games that were $130 and more random stuff that he just didn't need. $50 here, $100 there. He also keeps telling me about his investment accounts that he opened. So he HAD the money, he just chose to spend it on fun things and opening a Charles Schwab account when he doesn't have Charles Schwab money, rather than his car. When I brought that up he said he \"didn't have a reason until now to get his car fixed\" and now he \"doesn't have the money.\" I honestly think he was waiting around for me to buy the part for him. And now he says I am jeopardizing his job by not letting him use my car because now he doesn't have time to get it fixed and he doesn't have the money. He says that partners help each other and we are supposed to be a partnership. But to me, a partner doesn't constantly use their girlfriend as a safety net because they're irresponsible. AITA here?", "prompt_sha256": "a314fe80c06c3decb85fa923851d0766c9191c2255c1d0e30d8ac5cf0553302e", "body_sha256": "9030d8ff3120f6978a83851b76414277315deead421a6f47cad404df13e90ac8", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P043", "submission_id": "f6n1b1", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nTLDR:My friend has been struggling with drugs and alcoholism, so I'm trying to get her newborn son into a foster home.\n\nFor some background, I am a 32 year old female, my friend is 33 years old. I have been friends with her for 16 years and I realize she has been struggling lately with problems to her health, including drugs and alcohol.\n\nIt was 1 year ago that my friend had her baby, and as much as I am happy for her I cannot allow the child to be growing up in an environment where he is at constant risk to his health and being neglected by his mother.\n\nThe father has been gone since before he was born, and with a mother on dangerous substances, I feel like I should be fighting to get the baby out of this environment. \n\nSo Reddit, am I the asshole for trying to get my friends baby out of there?", "prompt_sha256": "b59c92b376969f30e8af364808ac575e38164482a527bd38e72737d458f90b56", "body_sha256": "9b44db6137abaac4944b9cd82bd76f62f7e8e3dc5526339601b1ef14c59c465a", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P044", "submission_id": "emch4u", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI'm in high school, my dad is in his 50s and my stepmom is in her 30s. (Yeah it's as weird as it sounds) They have an infant son who cries all the time. Kinda sucks because I'm really stressed about school, this year is really important for my college admissions.\n\nI'm really into camping and the outdoors. Making forest shelters by hand with stuff I find in the woods, camping, hiking, etc. (Like the primitive technology YouTube channel, but not as good lol). I've been camping and backpacking ever since I was little, with my mom.\n\nMy dad's house is on a lot of land and I've made a bunch of forest shelters out there, over the years, it's a hobby of mine. I know it's weird, but it's fun and relaxing. In the past, my dad had never had issues with me camping out there to test them out, or whatever.\n\nAnyway, I hadn't been getting much sleep at all with my halfbrother and stepmom here. He cries all day and night, and she's an early waker who makes a racket first thing in the morning.\n\nSo thr last few months I've been camping more and more. It's cold but I have a really good subzero sleeping bag, i can make a fire, I'm comfortable. And I sleep like a log; I've always slept well in the woods and it's a whole lot better than trying to sleep in the noisy house.\n\nIt's causing such a fuss for no reason, my dad is saying he doesn't like the idea of me sleeping out there alone in the winter, and I said to him that he never had a problem with it before, he's been letting me do it for years alone and it's always been OK, it's not fair for him to take it back because he's probably mad I'm the only one getting any sleep.\n\nMy stepmom says it's disrespectful, my dad puts a roof over our heads and I go to sleep in my little forts every night? That it's like what a child would do, not a young lady. \n\nThey haven't stopped me yet but I'm worried they will. I also don't see at all how I've done anything disrespectful but maybe there's just something I'm not getting?\n\nAITA for sleeping outside?", "prompt_sha256": "497f2d2901776bc813a5e1571b4008a7910255d1991c4e32e74fa041ed919c7b", "body_sha256": "607acec4fd12dd6f635de6d96a57b1b9a7cdc8c5b5285f7a59b7a7e9fdb9d222", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P045", "submission_id": "1d9o2ie", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThrowaway for privacy. I’m 21F. \n\nAs a post-graduation trip, me and my friends are going on a trip to France next summer. This is my first time going to Europe so I’m really excited, and we’re currently in the planning stage. This issue concerns one of my friends, Katie (also 21F). \n\nKatie has never been out of the country, and somehow she’s gotten it in her head that the worst thing someone can be in another country is a tourist. I think she’s read too many articles and watched too many tiktoks about how Europeans hate American tourists. Anyways, she’s now trying to change our trip to be as un-touristy as possible. For example, she’s sent the rest of the group pictures of French street fashion and is insisting that we can only pack outfits that look like it. When one person said she didn’t have clothes that looked like that, Katie just said “guess you’ll need to go shopping.” She also says that Europeans do not wear sneakers and will immediately label us as tourists if we’re seen wearing them, so we can’t bring them (even though we’ll be walking a lot). \n\nAdditionally, when I tried to suggest places for us to visit (Eiffel Tower, Louvre, Versailles, etc), Katie immediately shot them down and said that those are too “touristy” and we should try and find other places to go. When I asked her what kinds of places, she pulled up some French residential neighborhoods and local shops and said we would be better off spending our time there since it’s more “authentic.” To be clear, she’s not concerned about avoiding pickpockets since we’ve already purchased pickpocket-proof pouches. It’s JUST about “looking like tourists.” \n\nIn my view, there’s nothing wrong with being a tourist and doing touristy things as long as we’re respectful of the locals and French culture. Besides, if I’m only getting a limited time in France, I don’t want to be spending it all just walking around random people’s houses and looking at them like they’re zoo animals. I told this to Katie and she got upset and said I was the reason why Europeans hate tourists so much. I told her we ARE tourists, why try to hide it? I’m pretty sure French people would be MORE annoyed if we tried to act like locals instead of just being respectful visitors. \n\nKatie got even more upset and said that if I want to be disrespectful of French culture so bad, I can go to France on my own time. She then left our planning session. \n\nThe rest of our group is kind of split on this issue. Most of them agree with me and think it’s a waste of time to walk around residential neighborhoods instead of seeing the Eiffel Tower and the Louvre, but they also are very afraid of being perceived as annoying Americans. So I’d like to get some more perspectives on if I’m TA here. ", "prompt_sha256": "bef48233304c55c2cb16328acdb7932f40f9068f5a35e5fa50eca822c3243f9f", "body_sha256": "76915093750187cc77f94b0ee46febaceb7c3bc0175592d959f5a84ce0eb7a96", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P046", "submission_id": "16a1sd1", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHey everybody. This sounds kind of stupid to me but maybe my perspective is wrong.\r  \n\r  \nMy friend/roommate (M30's) who we can call Kevin has an 11-year old daughter who we can call Rachel. For context purposes, she has no physical disabilities or bladder control issues. She doesn't live with us full time but she does come every other weekend and on some weekends for visitation. Every time she does, she's always expecting people to do a lot of stuff for her that she could do herself such as 'my dad will carry my stuff/get my drinks/plate my food/give me some of his drink/food after I finished mine because he loves me'. This came to the point where Kevin actually (finally) told her last night that she can stop coloring for long enough to get her own water. We live in a 2 bedroom apartment with 1 bathroom.\r  \n\r  \nWhen I (F20's) went in this morning to brush my teeth, Rachel came over and said she needed to use the bathroom; I told her to wait and that she can't try to kick me out every time she wants to pee (this was at least the fourth time she's done so this weekend). Kevin tried to tell me that I should leave so that she can use the bathroom because using the toilet takes priority over everything else. To be clear, she came in while I was already in the process and not asking once she saw me. She waited for a maximum of two and a half minutes.\r  \n\r  \nOnce I was out, Kevin and I had a brief discussion in which he expressed that he felt it was inappropriate for me to make either him or Rachel wait when I was not physically using the toilet. My stance is that if someone is doing a short task, they are there first, and it is not an emergency, they should wait their turn. This seemed to be the common rule of shared bathrooms to me, but maybe I was wrong.\r  \n\r  \nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "bb1c8a8922b24833257ed1df1a26f8e5430ac5bb6750fd60c30dc3fdd2d2e798", "body_sha256": "2aed00c48ce93f37a2a2acb7382f71e8d225f624f51990657f37935c0476e4db", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P047", "submission_id": "1884xbf", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nWIBTA if I don't spend Xmas with my family?\n\nMy parents are looking after a family friends house and their dogs in another city over the xmas period. The expectation was that once we figured out work holidays etc that we would fly down and spend Xmas with them. I kind of just assumed that was the case, we loosely talked about it but it was always far away so no real plans were made. \n\nI called my mom the other day and said I was looking at flights, and would this date suit them etc for me and my girlfriend to come down. My mom acted all surprised, she said \"oh you didn't tell me she was going to come, I need to think about this\".\n\nI (male) have been with my gf for about 9 months. She has met my family before, even come on a weekend holiday with us. There was no drama at all, it went really well.\n\nLater my mom emailed me and said \"I'm so sorry, it's been a really tough year, your dad was in and out of hospital, I just want a relaxed Xmas with just the family and not have to worry about anyone else. I'm sorry for the position this puts you in as you have already told your gf She can come\"\n\nI don't know what to do. I feel my mom is being incredibly selfish. I have never been in a position where my partners parents have said they don't want me there, so I think this is incredibly rude of my mom. What does she expect, in the future she can just dictate things and not invite my girlfriend to family events? What if we get married? Is she going to be \"that\" mother in law that excludes my partner if she has the opportunity?\n\nI just feel like I can't be bothered flying down to be with my family and just making up some excuse about work and not going", "prompt_sha256": "ab9235df594033e1ce396a80319bf8a905ae1a6a5442361035cc6056172a9959", "body_sha256": "ce669e74abee76f11236ff0fc0322be751881cdb8a28e8bb952e4a079f3542dd", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P048", "submission_id": "1k6749o", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy husband (33 male) and me (29 female) got married almost a year ago. We never went away on a honeymoon as money was tight. For our 1 year anniversary my husband booked us a 4 day trip 5 hours away from home. Here is the backstory. I am a full time caregiver for his grandma, she fell a couple months ago spraining her ankle. Since getting home from the hospital she has been working really hard to get strong again. To also help me she gets PSWs 3 times a day. Her morning PSW bathes and gives her morning pills, afternoon PSW gives her a change and feeds her lunch. The night PSW gives her one last change and her nighttime pills. I do her workouts and change her when needed. (There can be 5-6 hours difference for the PSW sometimes) I also make sure that lunch and dinner are ready for when the PSWs get there. Grandma can walk herself to the living room (with someone behind her with her wheelchair in case she needs to sit down) and can use the washroom. My MIL also lives with us. She is on an oxygen tank, but still smokes cigarettes. She’s told me multiple times “it grosses her out if she has to change her” I told her it was the same for me, but she says “yeah, but I know you can do it” Anyway, she told us she was fine with us going away as she knows we didn’t go away after our wedding and has the PSWs coming. She also said she was getting a friend to help if needed. Since then she has changed her mind and asked us if we could shorten our trip. We wouldn’t be getting our money back from our booking, so I told her she would need to pay us back half of what we spent (it was 800$) so she would be paying us 400$ When I told her this she got very upset with me, rolling her eyes. Saying “I don’t have that kind of money. It would take me a while to pay it” I told her that was fine. She again rolled eyes and stopped talking to me. So, am I the asshole? ", "prompt_sha256": "81c79e8ffd2c3b7c87b297330388d16cc084ff503decd54f4f2f1b295406ba33", "body_sha256": "367524ef6264eeaab5fa6d437813509ce4d5095f920074c28a1554e2c88dd53d", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P049", "submission_id": "17uj65r", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nYesterday, I took my mom to the grocery store and my car had 3 fuel bar, and I was it will be fine for me to drive there and back and still have plenty of gas. \n\nYesterday my girlfriend asked me if I put gas on the car and I told her no. She was upset about it, and said I should have filled it up. I told her I didn’t go to the gas station.\n\nToday, she called upset because I didn’t put gas on the car yesterday, and I don’t want to do anything for her.\n\nI bought this car 5 years ago, and she is the one using it. I don’t need it for my job. I pay for the car note, insurance, and any repairs that needs to be done. \n\nAm I an asshole for not put gas on the car?", "prompt_sha256": "332a550fabe48b1a8ef645450dfed6681a33b29fc12f6e1e656080179cfd610c", "body_sha256": "0fd5c12b2d5d2b8860642f0d237c9151fd9b9fe9b34d550b72ceb2c551cbb739", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P050", "submission_id": "1gbj8i8", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (F24) am getting married to my fiancé (M26) next month and I have not invited any members of my family.\n\nMy roommate (F23) is very much a family person and invites her parents and two brothers round nearly every month. I have nothing against this as I enjoy spending time with them all, but in the 3.5 years we’ve known each other my roommate has consistently asked me if I’ll be inviting my parents around anytime soon. \n\nI cut off all contact with my family at 18 after moving out when I was more or less financially stable due to religious abuse. I won’t go into it, but I was asked to leave on multiple occasions as a minor to ‘clear my body and mind of sins’, and regular physics punishments were put in place when prayers where not long enough and bible verses were not memorised. I do not speak to any of them including my extended family, and I am perfectly content with this arrangement. \n\n I have explained this to my roommate but she doesn’t seem to understand that I genuinely don’t want to speak to them anymore. Our arguement about this haven’t been too disputed until about a month ago when we started discussing wedding invitations; I mentioned that I would only be inviting some good friends and a few of my co-workers, but she was clearly not happy about this. There were many conversations about how I probably misinterpreted my family’s abuse as an attempt at education and sharing culture. \n\nTo wrap it up, I’m getting married soon and my roommate is attempting to postpone it until I sort things out with my parents. My fiancé is on my side completely and has said he’ll support me no matter what. However, some part of me kind of agrees with my roommate’s words; if I was a parent, I’d be incredibly upset to hear that my child got married and didn’t invite me to the wedding. What am I supposed to do? \n\nApologies for any bad formatting, I’m on mobile. ", "prompt_sha256": "c6b7b60858284b743921bb7b589f003c450dec1d6246b479f50bae0b0907f999", "body_sha256": "150a50cbd8ec58d12a06f7f0c6c2331fce8bbc62203aa7e1c225d65cb25a4880", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P051", "submission_id": "1anhrtb", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy roommate and I got really into this one singer. Since she moved in really quickly and has always been on time with rent, I decided to surprise her with tickets to the singer's show. They were pretty good seats for only being $300 each. We were having a good time, as much as some of the people there were kind of being obnoxious. Out of nowhere, during a really quiet part, my roommate yelled \"Mother is mothering\" and literally everybody around us started yelling at her to shut up, shut the F up, etc. I straight up told my roommate to never do that again and that she embarrassed me a ton. I apologized to everybody around me and explained I had no idea she would do something like that.\n\nWhen we got home, I told her to pay me back for the ticket because she ruined the show for me. She told me she was not \"obligated\" to, and that this is just how concerts are these days. I told her that because of her, a bunch of strangers cussed at me. She started yelling, saying that people cussed at her, too, and that I was making this all about me. I told her this literally would not have happened if she had concert etiquette like a normal person, and she stormed off and sent me the money, whining about how she had to ask her dad. And I guess she told all of our friends a completely different story, because I got a bunch of texts saying I was a bad friend and that I was using her for money or whatever.\n\nEventually, somebody uploaded that exact moment, my roommate found it, and she basically shut herself in her room since then because of her \"mental health.\" AITA, not for telling her off for the \"Mother\" crap, but because I made her pay me back for her ticket?", "prompt_sha256": "1e01018a8b1aa1d4ffeb378b81ed8fdd9820f46e485348fcd3e0c40d31517207", "body_sha256": "705546e19a7e14ad17e69fa55561e52b3a2db13434b7ebd70437a5533b85bbcd", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P052", "submission_id": "x5z3rr", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (18f) lost my mom when I was 4yrs old. She had issues with depression before she was pregnant with me &amp; it got worse when I was born. She was a teen mom too with not a lot of support, so I think that just piled up and she couldn’t handle it anymore. She and my dad weren’t together when she died, but ik he loved her a lot, even if they were really young. Her parents still feel really guilty about it all, so they pretty much just let my dad raise me on his own without any input/visitation from them. So I don’t have contact with my mom's side of the family except for her older sister, my aunt (37f).\n\nMy dad (34m) met his wife Mel (33f) when I was 10. She’s really sweet, and even before she and my dad were together, she’d take me out sometimes just the two of us to go get our nails done or go shopping. My dad did a good job on his own, don't get me wrong, but it was nice to have a woman around to do those stereotypical girl things with. When they started dating, Mel still made sure to include me, and when they got married and later had my baby brother (3m) that never changed. I love her a lot, and I feel really fortunate to have her in mine and my dad’s life. She makes him really happy.\n\nSo we have an assignment in my media class where the girls make a video with their moms. We basically interview our mom and ask her what she wished for her future daughter like dreams and stuff and then have a conversation comparing that with how we turned out. I obviously can’t do that with my mom, so I asked my teacher if I could have my stepmom do it instead, and he said that was fine.\n\nI was catching up with my aunt at a coffee place like we do every other Saturday and she saw the paper detailing the project because it fell out of my bag. She ended up reading it and seeing how I had changed some of the sample questions to apply to my stepmom instead of my mom, and she started to get really upset.\nShe said it wasn’t right of me to include Mel in a project specifically for mothers and their daughters, and that Mel shouldn’t have made herself a maternal figure in my eyes because that was erasing my mom.\nI tried telling her that Mel wasn’t trying to erase my mom at all, and that I hadn’t even asked her about doing the project with me yet, but my aunt said that we were disrespecting my mother’s memory. We both left the coffee shop pretty upset, and later when I was home my aunt ended up texting my dad and blowing up at him for allowing his wife to take mom’s place in my life. Mel even sat me down this morning and told me that she would never ever want to replace my mom.\n\nI feel awful for all of this. I wanted to include her in the project bc I love her. I didn’t mean to make anyone feel bad. Am I TA for wanting to do the project with Mel?", "prompt_sha256": "1bc76cea58815faeb916eec23ef9d6177c10eef5748b8ed3d053064b134fe4b7", "body_sha256": "3b6b93f7c068680ae0d20cbecf9a49113311ee7c6462f876d9b6f5ffc99eda39", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P053", "submission_id": "15sbold", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHey Reddit, I need some honest opinions here. So recently I (19F) got pregnant (I'm 11 weeks now) and so far the only people that I had told (before this whole situation happened) were my best friend (20M) and my parents. I was planning on eventually telling our entire friend group altogether the next time we hung out. Well, about a week ago my best friend told me that he's going to propose to his girlfriend who is also in our friend group. His idea was really romantic and thoughtful, and I am so excited for them. He has been apparently planning it for months and he told me he's going to propose to her during a picnic and also invite everyone in the friend group to be there as well. Here's where things went south though...\n\nSo a bit of explanation about my mindset before I say what happened. After he told me he was going to propose to her I started thinking what people would think about me if he proposed to his girlfriend and I soon after that told all of our friends that I was pregnant, which I was already planning to do very soon. I was thinking everyone would think I was trying to take the attention away from our newly engaged friends. So I figured the better alternative was to say it first, before he proposed.\n\nSo the day of the proposal arrives and we (our friend group) lay the picnic blanket down and start chatting and eating at this beautiful park that my best friend chose for us to go to. No one knows about the proposal except for me and him. I see my best friend stand up and I can tell he's about to get down on his knee so I say \"I have some news to share with you all\" and I tell everyone I'm going to have a baby. Everyone except for my best friend smiled and congratulated me. We spent the picnic talking about my plans for my baby shower and what the nursery would look like and yada yada, and my best friend was quiet almost the entire time, looking at me with a grumpy expression on his face.\n\nLater he texted me telling me that I completely ruined his proposal and asking me why I would do that to him. I gave him my reasoning, telling him I did it as to not take all the attention but he responded that I did take all the attention. But I didn't because soon he is going to propose to his girlfriend and he will be the new topic that everyone is talking about. If anything I believe I did him a solid. He called me a bunch of colorful names and said he is considering cutting me off for what I did. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "13cf79250db460a15cb02abab3dcf47dbbec92aba79f0211b23140a88be8df8c", "body_sha256": "8db0d22cb7ebebfef55460ba0476dd0679541c5261fc3b6d1ee8708fbb996dca", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P054", "submission_id": "13mdzxw", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy wife and I have pre-teen triplets who we take on vacation every year.\n\nCritical information is that while we share finances, she makes about 3 times what I do and we (or more accurately she) uses her bonus each year for vacations. She is happy to do this as far as I know. \n\nThis year I suggested Colorado. Not only is it one of the most beautiful areas in our country, but I happened to be stationed there many years ago. Also, it would provide me with the opportunity to spend time with, and possibly say goodbye to one of my closest friends who has stage 4 liver cancer.\n\nI expressed my wish to spend some quality time with him as she was booking the trip. She stated we weren't going to fly all the way there just to hang out at his house and planned many activities for the week. \n\nWe just got home from this trip and due to her scheduling activities for the vast majority of the time, I got to see my friend cumulatively for less than half of a day. \n\nAnd to clarify, she would not have been comfortable taking the kids to any of the activities without me.\n\nHe just texted me to thank me for visiting, but expressed some frustration that we had so little time together. I shared the same feeling, as it may be the last time I see him.\n\nWIBTA for telling her I'm upset that she didn't allocate more time for me to see him? I'm already question myself because we went on \"her dime\".\n\nETA - he has an in-ground pool and stuff in his back yard, so a day or two there wouldn't have been \"boring\".", "prompt_sha256": "7693b6fed9004ac61d060e29eaac0cd9d568890286db86b00d31d95bab910e29", "body_sha256": "c079e0bd9d9bdc749a0ccd4715b7378552fcf27b599a0e21f4c1347414968d49", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P055", "submission_id": "upn4ht", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nThe title sounds bad but please hear me out. \n\nI (16M) have a best friend (15F Ella) who has been sent weird comments by a guy (16M Dave) \n\nMe and Ella met some people back in 2020 in our city from another school and a little later we started meeting up with these people on the regular. It was a pretty big group, and Dave was part of this group. Around this time Ella was really into cosplay and she’d cosplay many anime characters, in the best way I can put it is all these characters are girls popular amongst male fans. You can kinda imagine what it is. Now something I have to mention is Ella is a lesbian but she is very feminine, so she enjoyed cosplaying these characters regardless. The issue starts because Dave starts jokingly calling her his “Waifu” whenever we would meet up, it would make Ella uncomfortable but she never said anything to keep the peace in the group. The comments started increasing and Dave would start dming Ella about a year later after all this. In that year at one point Ella kept making polite remarks saying she does not like men to sort of keep him at bay but nothing. She hates confrontation and simply decided to suck it up to not lose the rest of her friends.\n\nFast-forward February of this year and Ella decides to block Dave everywhere and stop hanging out with the group. We had already sort of drifted away from everyone else for irrelevant reasons and she decided to just move on. During this time I started going to parties and gatherings were Dave was. He was at almost every single party. He came up to me at 1 and said something along the lines of “Dude I def made Ella question.” After this I kept my distance. Another time, I heard him talking to a friend who was telling him that she wasn’t interested in him and that she was a lesbian and he said “Just wait till I catch her off guard.” from that day on I didn’t interact with him and just ignored him.\n\nOne day I was at a party he was at, and he came up to me and said he was going to my school and that he’d finally make Ella his. I told her everything and she was mad. She told me As soon as she sees him she’ll say everything she’s wanted to say all along. I was ok with that but I realized if she did that it would put my connections with him at stake and I didn’t want that. If that happened his friends wouldn’t hang out with me again.\n\nI told her and she was angry. From now on she’s been giving me the silent treatment and all my friends in our group have sided with her and haven’t spoken to me. I’m starting to think I didn’t do the right thing by protecting him because of my connections, so please let me know AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "9b1b00828563cc5f5ed4dd31ca6be1207c2dbd091a565c9d5dc59b31b6191b6c", "body_sha256": "07e7bd254d79ed472cf826c8fcab9f88662b25fab35290feac0e0ccea17cc9d7", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P056", "submission_id": "vivygh", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI female 24, have an older sister “Sarah” (33), for years growing up Sarah has always thought she’s better than everyone, she has a group of friends that she likes to talk a lot of crap about but then be nice to their face. \n\nMy partner (m26) and I have been dating for 5 years, we are in no way financially ready for being engaged/married as we are saving for a house that we’d like to buy. \n\nwe were all at a family dinner at our grandparents when Sarah decided to kick up about how my partner hasn’t proposed to me (we have spoke about it before) and that she thinks it’s time that we start settling down to have a wedding and children, I told her that we were not interested in that right now as we had plans — she began to act like my 5 year old nephew, stomping her feet at the dinner table, she had made the remark saying that she only wanted to see if our wedding would be better than her own wedding that she had 3 years ago. She likes to compare things. \n\nRecently I had decided to throw a dinner for friends and family, everything was going well, everyone was getting along. While I was in the kitchen making food, Sarah decided to come in and “help me” by leaning against the side while I prepared vegetables for our meals. I was enjoying the quiet until she turned to me and said that I would make such a cute couple with my good friend, and that we would look so good together, this had taken me back asking her what she had meant by this, her reaction was to snicker and say “I meant what I said” indicating that she wanted to start something in my own home. \n\nI decided that enough was enough and told her to get out and not to come back, when she left with my brother-in-law my parents turned on me saying that I had overreacted and that it was only a joke and that I shouldn’t take it to heart. AITA for kicking her out?", "prompt_sha256": "06c8732d013bd4ac2e0110162bba7d76f5578d721d30eede24db22fb54ae402a", "body_sha256": "734dff2ecb45806dcc40fa4795e67f0fa0ba3742c47750c1b64050f73ffb4ba0", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P057", "submission_id": "1ititx6", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n  About once every week (or every two weeks  depending on life factors) I smoke half or so of a pre -roll on my apartment’s patio. I only ever have dispensary bought pre-rolls, and I never buy any flower itself. \n\n  Usually I will smoke between midnight-3am, and never earlier than 11PM, to avoid bothering anyone with a smell that can definitely be strong and putrid to some. I’m usually outside for 15-30 minutes maximum, and I barely finish half of a pre-roll before I’m at a level I’m happy with. After smoking I will spray a spurt or two of Ozium which to my nose clears the smell, however I know that I’m probably used to the smell. \n\n  There is another unit with a patio directly above mine. One night a few weeks ago I was mid-smoke at about 2 am when I hear my upstairs neighbor ask me to smoke somewhere else as they have their patio door open (The weather was nice for once). I replied “sorry about that”, as it kind of shocked and startled me. I heard a slight annoyed groan and heard him then slam his door shut. \n\n  I put it out immediately and then sprayed some ozium and went inside. I’ve been too nervous to smoke since, even though I had done it for at least a year without ever hearing anything. I have no real way of telling if my upstairs neighbor has their window open or not, the way the building is shaped the only door is their sliding glass patio door directly above mine which I can’t see from my unit. \n\nI’ve thought about leaving a note so I could talk to my neighbor personally about this, and hopefully come up with a compromise of sorts (i.e. he just texts me when he wants to have his windows open, not to ask me but just to tell me) but I’m slightly nervous since he definitely seemed to be aggressive from the way he talked to me. \n\n  I’ve also thought about just smoking again on a night with temps that most people wouldn’t have any windows open. \n\nAITA for this? Could or should I be doing more? I don’t want to be inconsiderate to my neighbors, but I enjoy smoking once every so often, and I feel I have the right to that in moderation. ", "prompt_sha256": "a53330f4f5bd2535e85533970cc62df51f6587e4fcaecc9d53439c65d5a93a80", "body_sha256": "aa5d7387394642d5e1daed30b0ca48ba83ff24e437f2a921fe2e17f3a327a421", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P058", "submission_id": "g4u5t7", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nAm I an asshole for pushing a ladies dog with my foot?\n\nThis is my first post ever! So In my hometown there is a specific restaurant I really enjoy going to even when I’m alone. It is a sit down restaurant with a laid back atmosphere, anyway at the time I was with 2 of my buddies. I am severely asthmatic and with this condition comes extreme allergies that affect my body in more ways than just sniffles. If I get bad allergies it makes my lungs swell then all of a sudden I cannot breathe and have to go to the hospital. Anyway my worst allergies is to dogs and while they are cute I’m just extremely allergic to them and cannot be near them at all. So at this restaurant some lady walks in for pickup and she had a dog(big dog like really furry idk dog breeds well) and my buddies asked if they could play with the dog and the woman said sure. I stay seated and make no indication I want to touch the dog when it starts to come up to me (this dog is young too and very hyper it just jumped up on my friends too) so instinctively I put my foot up to block it from getting to me and I pushed it away with my foot gently. The woman yells at me saying not to kick her dog and got all flustered, even my friends say I was a dick and should never do that to a dog. I’m just confused. Am I the asshole?", "prompt_sha256": "1aa8ec22a816fb8603dd611e6ce5877587f1acf2c635efbc21276030a5c4d5cd", "body_sha256": "afc504e4c0ba03f8c365065ae2cda3f38181cc55c83dadf7f702e82279aac25b", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P059", "submission_id": "16rbiwm", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHi all, this is my first post here. My partner and I went to an art fair this afternoon that was very cute and fun. We bought a couple prints and earrings, and my partner suggested looking at this one vendor who sold pastel earrings. They wanted to buy me some, but none of them were really what I wanted, so I passed on them. We went over a second time by my partner’s request to look again and see if I wanted any. Again, I said I wasn’t really feeling them and we moved on. After walking around through some other shops and getting snacks, my partner and I walked back to the fair where they said “Now this isn’t negotiable, I really want to get you a pair of earrings from that vendor”. Thinking they were joking, I once again said that I wasn’t feeling them and we walked back to the car. They didn’t seem upset at first, but as we drove home they said that it wasn’t about me, it was about them buying me a gift. They compared me to their parents in that I shut them down after they said it was non-negotiable, and that I didn’t let them do something they wanted to do. Then they were silent the rest of the way home, and are now in their room with the door shut. We were having a great day up until this moment, and I want to know if I was in the wrong for telling them that I didn’t want the gift. Should I have been okay with them spending money for me on something I didn’t want?", "prompt_sha256": "2c30bc3c2dfd2e5453f1ea1e61a692d17674483fdf63c9b934c117c3deb835fb", "body_sha256": "4c14e579486b77160f79070a9223565090d4c1aea8877a590628e4848220155f", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P060", "submission_id": "ghfs1j", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy parents and extended family are extremely physically affectionate, and it makes me extremely uncomfortable even when it’s the smallest thing. When someone touches my arms or my head without warning I start trying to get them off me, and I naturally flinch away when it comes to my legs and back. I’ve told them many times I don’t like being touched but no one really takes me seriously except for my cousin. Sometimes if something feels like it was too much it sends me into a minor panic attack or just makes me cry when i’m alone and think about it, and I can’t sleep because I feel like someone’s trying to ‘get me’ if that makes sense.\n\nI’ve been told by my dad this makes my family feel bad and unless i’ve been s/xually ab/sed, which I’m very fortunate to have not been, I shouldn’t be reacting this way, and that I shouldn’t be so uptight about physical contact and just tough it out. I don’t know what is wrong with me, and asking a therapist hasn’t been any help. Am I the Asshole for wanting to tell them to leave me out of their touching and hugging?\n\n(This is my first time actually posting on reddit, sorry if I did something wrong lol, I normally just browse but I wanted to see if I could get outside opinions on this since it’s been bugging me for a while)", "prompt_sha256": "4fb62a4a1c74cf2a3a4734cd98ec1353f95f5980fc3c87ad1a9c0fdafc50be01", "body_sha256": "5d5ee0ca6c33dc3e51e0a18d26089dd66c933f2fd30c9fc0a4c1c4f32f65dff0", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P061", "submission_id": "k5x6ub", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy ex’s family are wealthy, and each child/grandchild gets a trust fund. His grandfather is very conservative though and doesn’t consider illegitimate children as part of the family. So, when my ex and I found out I was pregnant, he insisted we tell everyone we had gotten back together and were engaged. \n\nHis family still weren’t happy since we weren’t married but my ex has always been his grandfathers’ favourite so our son got all of the benefits any other (great)grandchild would get. \n\nMy stepsister mentioned how shocked she was my ex and I got back together since I had told her I hated him after we broke up and I admitted the truth to her. We were close so I didn’t think she would tell anyone else. Well, she went and told my ex’s family and now they’re angry at both of us. They obviously think I’m an AH now and have been very vocal about it. My ex’s grandfather also isn’t talking to him now and my ex is blaming me, so I feel bad.\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e92dd542dbc2536469da955a998a0d01ad1b951b1fa477c034022669dc058090", "body_sha256": "cc377738942bdb56bcc0ba84d49b33c18360ea566e75eef315c0bef6c79e37cb", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P062", "submission_id": "kqf3ro", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nThrowaway.\n\nMy nephew, Max is 17 years old. He's my nephew (24 here btw) and I love him dearly but he is a bit of a spoiled brat. He goes through phases like all kids/teens do and seems to have a different interest every month. A few months ago, it was reptiles. He'd stayed with me whilst my sister was in hospital (all fine now) and got really fascinated by my animals, in particular, my red footed tortoise, Daisy.\n\nHe begged his mum to get him one and eventually she gave in. Three months later, Max had a baby horsefield. He was so into looking after his tortoise for about a month and then I'm guessing the novelty wore off. From what I saw on the pictures he'd post online, the little guy didn't have a UV light. His heat lamp also broken after a month which Max never bothered to replace. I got a bit worried and spoke to my sister about it. I explained the importance of the lighting in his enclosure and also brought up that the table he was in looked a little small, even for a baby tort. My sister is not a heartless person so she warned Max that if his behaviour didn't improve then she'd be giving the tortoise to someone who would look after him, she did pay for him after all.\n\nMax's behaviour did not improve. He wasn't spot cleaning the enclosure and had to be reminded to feed him. Eventually my sister had enough. She wanted to give him away to someone that could take care of him properly. I had a bit of room in my place and I still had Daisy's old table (I'd been hoping to buy another tortoise myself) and long story short, I took him in, I payed my sister the money for the tortoise but not the enclosure as I already had my own.\n\nLast week, Max texted me and asked for his tortoise back. He told me he'd done more research into tortoise care and that he was ready to take his tortoise back and to his credit he had done his research from what I could tell. But I refused. I do get that he's done his research but I don't trust him. Besides, I've already paid the money for him. Max and a handful of family members are accusing me of stealing  the little guy from him and some others have asked me to just give the tortoise back to avoid any drama.\n\nAITA?\n\neta - Thank you for all the support you guys. My internet went out last night because of the terrible weather so sorry for not replying to a  lot of comments. I don't generally take a lot of photos of my animals, or photos in general, so I can't post a picture of the little guy right now. He's burrowed down into the substrate right now but I'll try to get a picture of him for you guys when he wakes up :)", "prompt_sha256": "d5d5d1e2ac05de9ee3f4365b693670458d10f7720ee6420dc7706ac381dcbfc1", "body_sha256": "c8d568e4abade37bcb9c98adceb7e1a1bdafb2d71e15fee1797c58abc979d2f2", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P063", "submission_id": "rgaowv", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMe (f24) and husband (m27) had a new neighbour move in next door in June of this year, a single mother 'May' with two young boys (4 and 7). I don't know too much but know it was a bad situation so we offered to lend a hand whenever she needed, doing the occasional babysitting and school drop offs/pick ups, grocery shopping, etc. I am a SAHM with a 2m but recently had a baby at the beginning of December so had been able to help out until the end of my pregnancy. \n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nWith Christmas approaching, I asked if we could buy the boys a present (last year she didn't have enough money so didn't celebrate and didn't even tell 4m it was Christmas). She said yes and was excited to celebrate Christmas, we even lent her some Christmas decorations. I got the two boys some Harry Potter lego, gift-wrapped it, and had my husband deliver it. \n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nLast weekend the boys came over really excited and were thanking me for the Christmas present. I asked them how they like it and told them why I picked it out (my nephew 7m has them and liked it) but 4m got confused and said their mother got them the lego and said I gave them clothes. I was a little slow (I blame baby brain and sleep deprivation) but my husband took over and 'saved it', claiming we knew they'd be more excited over toys than clothes. They didn't seem to question it before leaving and I forgot all about it.\n\n&amp;#x200B;\n\nThe next day May came over furious and began yelling about how I ruined her children's Christmas and had a white saviour complex and wanted all the credit and attention (they're black/mixed). She told me I should've never assumed she'd tell them I got the gift and claimed I did it on purpose getting such a 'good and expensive' gift. She said I should've given her all the credit and I tried to explain I didn't know and once I did we backtracked, but apparently 7m knew and now 4m did as well. I apparently should've known and wanted to give credit to her without her asking, and me not doing so 'said something about my character'. She was furious when she left and we haven't spoken since but it's been weighing on me ever since.", "prompt_sha256": "cfe62d1ffd20a04a4a4259573492f729253d2ccec2fbb5bf15d1996ce7bc3015", "body_sha256": "95853fc53f0c6ca4b1231516d562d3470299bebdb83c8951bb4eaf9c3cee3b93", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P064", "submission_id": "157n0o2", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy wife and I have a son that just turned 1 two days ago. We decided to celebrate by baking cupcakes and taking him on a stroller ride in the park where we had a picnic and some playtime/walking practice with our son. We chose not to get him any new presents, considering he’s only a baby and our house is bombarded with toys and clothes, and there’s nothing he really needs at the moment.\n\nMy MIL insisted to come with us so we let her, and she gifted him a $120 giant wooden activity cube. We appreciated it very much, even though it’s kind of obnoxious lol. We think he’ll play with it and enjoy it when he gets a little older if not now, and it’s all one piece so we don’t have to worry about lost pieces. We thanked her for the present, and then she asked us what we bought for our son, to which my wife said “we decided he didn’t need anything new, so the fun time and the cupcakes are his present.”. My MIL absolutely flipped out about this, saying that we “didn’t love or care about our son” and that we were “selfish negligent parents” for not buying a baby brand new toys that he didn’t need and will probably never play with. \n\nAs if that wasn’t bad enough, she started passive aggressively talking to us through our son, by saying to him in a baby voice, “do mommy and daddy not love you enough to get you new toys?” “You know that grandma will always buy you toys…”, etc. This made us both very angry, and I told her to stop talking to us though a baby. She continued to call us terrible parents and trying to make us feel guilty for not buying a baby who doesn’t even know he exists yet, new toys that he’ll never play with. \n\nWhen our son gets older, obviously we’ll buy him new stuff. But we didn’t feel that it was necessary this year because he loses toys so quickly and doesn’t even play with the ones he has. His favorite toy is a plastic bottle anyway. \n\nMy wife finally said “if you’re going to talk to us this way, you can leave. And if you don’t leave, we will.”.\n\nWe were sick of arguing with her, so we packed up our things and left. My MIL keeps texting me and my wife and trying to ask if she can babysit our son, and we haven’t responded. \n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e1ddc5485c308b2a9c211fdb8c261cae7d74a32a55288f1678d9e932926d400e", "body_sha256": "a4896a877e1a737ddc873cc09fd8d4e0ec4daf2856ce9d78768e402f4d2b47ac", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P065", "submission_id": "xyy8zd", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI(28F) am white and is marrying a man(31M) of Indian descent. To respect both family’s traditions we are having two weddings. Me and my fiancé are splitting the budget for the white wedding and the Indian wedding is being paid for by his parents on their insistence. Originally we were supposed to have the white wedding first followed by a traditional Indian wedding. Now, that the wedding is less two months away, my MIL informs me that she had to prepone the Indian wedding because some people from her side of the family can’t attend anymore on the original date because of some issues making it take place before the white wedding. While wedding planning, I was told by my future MIL that during the Indian wedding I have to apply mehendi ( a sort of temporary tattoo) on my hands. I said okay. The thing is, if my Indian wedding happens before the white wedding, I would have by hands covered with the temporary tattoos and it would totally clash with my wedding theme, so I informed my future MIL that I do not like the idea of having the mehendi put on anymore. She was upset to say the least and also implied that since she’s paying for the wedding, she should have the right to decide. She said I was disrespecting the customs and acting ignorant. I talked with my fiancé about it and even though he didn't say it outright, I know he agrees with his mother. My friends are divided. Some think that I am right to want a specific aesthetic while others think I’m being worrying over nothing. I have had little to no say about what happens at the Indian wedding so I really want the white wedding to be exactly how I want it.\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "1a4ce515109867522f305260b833ed18ceaf38d85f8147d6c6f179b28595410e", "body_sha256": "d443d160b784c7323ea9a168839a1e731df49db468ee105140168d986ce683f0", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P066", "submission_id": "nj91d3", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nContext: My \\[16m\\] aunt and uncle are divorced, my aunt lives abroad and my uncle is very ill in hospital. My cousin “Lucy” \\[18f\\] is an only child. My parents are also divorced, my brother “John” \\[14m\\] and I live with our mother. Staying with my father is not an option. John has aspergers. John and I each have our own rooms. \n\nSituation: While my \\[16m\\] uncle is in hospital, my cousin “Lucy” \\[18f\\] will be staying with us. However, we - my mother, brother “John” and I - live in a small bungalow with only three rooms. My mother works shifts and John is very particular about having his own personal space, so my mother wants me to share my room with Lucy while she is here. I have no personal issues with Lucy particularly but I am uncomfortable sharing my room with a teenage girl. The lack of privacy concerns me. My mother says it shouldn’t matter because ‘we’re family’ but it still makes me uncomfortable. I know that this is a tough situation for everyone and that it probably won’t make a great impression if Lucy is asked to sleep in the living room, but we don’t know how long she’ll be here for and I like my space. AITA for not being willing to share?", "prompt_sha256": "29a892bc2ceaa3987333fa42604e1c3390c3b4a81f311f2b1b687f5f1a133672", "body_sha256": "80564b5a63acd36887f9c27b904798d48198c216f38a3381d1dc65d2f2871e85", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P067", "submission_id": "k33sle", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI(25F) am getting married to T(32F). We’re not sure when anymore because of Covid and finances and xyz,. But recently we started ring shopping, and decided that ASAP when it’s safe to have people together- we’re going for it.\n\nT and I have basically talked about getting married since we hit 6months of dating. We are hopelessly in love, and have been now for almost 3 years. But ever since we qued family in to the idea, step sister: C (24F) raised issues with us.\n\nThe first, was C tried to pressure T and I to wait atleast a year after she had planned to get married to have our own wedding. (This ended up being what we wanted due to the virus, but she pulled in my dad and step mom to try and get them to talk to us about how unfair it would be for us to get married in the same year.)\n\nThen, once C’s wedding actually took place, she exposed everyone to Covid. C promised us that everyone was to wear masks (they did not.) and that it wasn’t going to be awkward with us being a lesbian couple in a conservative group, and if it was that she wouldn’t tolerate it. (It was, and she did. C even pushed my dad to ask T and I not to show any PDA, including hugging- and to introduce us as “friends” or “roomates,”)\n\nC’s asked us not to use any colors from her wedding scheme, and has sparked more than a few disagreements between me, my dad, and my step mom over things like registry gifts, finances, ceremony, the cake, ect,.\n\nI’m bordering telling the 3 of them that if they’re going to stress T and I out about the whole thing then none of them have to be involved. It would break my heart to think of not having my dad at my wedding or having him miss out on the role of father of the bride for pre-wedding stuff, especially over something so stupid and petty, but I can’t take any more of C’s instigating.\n\nI told my dad today that if C brings up anything else about T and I’s wedding with him to not talk to me about it, because I’m very seriously considering not inviting her. He told me he wanted me to be civil and turn the other cheek, smile for the appearances and what-have you to keep the peace because this girl is a constant ticking time bomb. I told him then that to be fair: it’s my wedding. And I don’t have to put up with her shit if I’m not marrying her. He asked that I think about it- and said he has to deal with  C and my step mom if that happens. \n\nWIBTA if I told just C not to come to our wedding Vs., if I told all 3 of them not to come?\nIdk what to do here.", "prompt_sha256": "0637b2a9e858257c427a4e66cbed3647150cabf8e267d762a542e681f30f9138", "body_sha256": "97dcde8626c14fb8e21d73933b8e0db17d0898c9a85aa454054e7a902685d4c6", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P068", "submission_id": "ou2fy3", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy wife and I have been together for 14 years and we have 2 daughters. In our dating phase we probably should have split. I was a closed book and didn't give the attention and affection she needed. But the way she treated me then was rough ngl.\n\nShe slept with a former good friend of mine right before we got married and this relationship for 2 years after we got married, compared him to me (even in terms of intimacy) unfavorably right after I found out about their affair and got an STI from it, mocked me as father and a husband for a year after while I begged her to go to counselling with me, and said I deserved it all for how I treated her like I was invisible and said I was lucky she didn't abandon me and take our first daughter (she's my bio child) away from me.  I deserved that treatment. I got it then and I get it now. I worked too much, played too much when I was at home instead of taking care of the house and didn't care to my wife's emotional and romantic needs well at all. I understood. Thankfully, a few years later, right after our second girl was born we got ourselves into therapy, individual (IC) and couples counselling and we are now much stronger.\n\nThe main problem of this post lies within me and her and her family. Lately, I have had some unfortunate side effects from the prior years. My IC has been a big help. But I have had ticks, like when someone tries to touch me I shudder suddenly and if I don't see them, I may react by shouting at them. I have compulsive issues when it comes to my family, I always make sure my wife and daughters are well fed and happy before they leave anywhere without me for instance. Also I can't stop weeping out of nowhere when I'm alone, like my mind goes to that dark place of myself being a failure. I have bad sleep cycles, like waking up in a sweat when I'm deep asleep in the middle of the night and sleeping more in the morning when I'm supposed to work.\n\nIt then comes to the wife's parents and sister being around a lot more, being grandparents and aunt to our daughters and helping them \"grow strong\" as my father-in-law says. One day, her sister saw me crying alone and told my wife what happened. My wife came into the room and yelled at me and I just sat there listening to her complain that I was supposed to be over our past already. Her parents overheard everything and said that I wasn't fit to be raising our kids like this. I repeatedly tell them for months I'm in therapy and getting treatment and they push me harder and say worried for our kids. They all came over once for dinner, and continued to push me when I was triggering. I snapped and said to shut the fuck up to my wife and her family, and that I couldn't take their reactions to my triggers. I then said I would get better if they just treated me like a human being. They looked at me like I was evil and left immediately. My wife is sleeping in another room for weeks now, and her family won't acknowledge me when they come over. AITA for how I reacted?", "prompt_sha256": "2db2ffd5a74edda63a4a7e7429086a847144cf07c714ad2d9a4bcb0dbed09fae", "body_sha256": "53acca05a561f040ad9cb2e54bc1fd208f063f482de85afd5db35c6ca36ee9e9", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P069", "submission_id": "1b7kuz9", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nHello everyone. My (29) husband (28) have been married for 6 months and we are already having major issues … the main one being his drinking.\n\nHe had an issue with alcohol and cocaine use in the past. When we first met we would drink every weekends and often take drugs together. Many of these evenings ended horrendously and our relationship has almost been destroyed on many occasions because of this. \n\nWe both saw how alcohol and drugs were affecting us and we cut down a lot. We still drank together occasionally but even then we would still argue. I will fully admit I can get very emotional when drinking, I have recognised that it’s really not good for me. So now I’ve decided to stop drinking. \n\nHowever my husband does not feel the same. He drinks beer pretty much every night. On average 5 large cans. I think this is excessive and I’m honestly sick of dealing with a drunk husband. He doesn’t really cause any trouble other than talking constantly about himself and disturbing me when he comes up to bed and I need to be up at 5am. He also grinds his teeth at night and when he drinks it gets worse; this is really affecting my sleep.\n\nHe recently quit his job and is only working Uber eats (most of the time we work together, he drives and I pick up orders) however it’s not bringing in much money and honestly I think he left work so he can stay up until 1am drinking and then get up whenever he likes.\n\nI’m super stressed because we are depending on his income right now. Every day is a struggle to pay our bills. I am looking for a job to fit in around my studies as a student nurse. I have a couple of interviews lined up. \n\nAlongside this, the drinking is sending me over the edge. I know he is feeling depressed and I am trying to support him but I feel like I’m losing my mind trying to hold everything together. He can be an extremely hardworking man, he would do anything for his family and when things are going well we are best friends and always have each others backs. He is trying to turn his life around after a very difficult few years and I don’t want to be too hard on him. He has big dreams but I can’t see how they will materialise. He can be a very messy and impulsive, we think he has ADHD.  \n\nWow I am sorry this is so long, I just don’t know if I should continue with him hoping that things will change. I feel like my life is going nowhere with him, which is an awful way to feel. Tonight I asked him to have a night off from drinking, he refused so I snapped and said I don’t want any alcohol in the house (it’s my house that we live in) and I said if you want to drink then you’ll have to do it somewhere else. So he left and I don’t know where he has gone. 😥\n\n", "prompt_sha256": "ec3c91d42dca34847cc0e417a8f438809f2ef5d26d37e8d6c13be7005957ab96", "body_sha256": "e1c2627c70837f86252f1f768703300e37504fd484ddf0ca66b5700fd2066a32", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P070", "submission_id": "1l0r032", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (36F) have recently had an argument with my mum (56F). Long story short, I have had enough of her \"helping\" me without asking first. Some of the \"help\" I received from her in the last 3 years was (bear with me):\n\n* Bringing homemade food (sometimes, we're grateful, but sometimes we've just made 3 days worth of food that cannot be frozen so we end up deciding which dish we throw away),\n* (Re)gifting clothes; gloves EVERY Christmas, oversized business clothes (I don't wear suits to work), kids clothes on sale (why would they even make white crawling overalls, have they seen a child?)..,\n* Inviting family members to get-togethers she does not host (I would be fine with them coming if she actually asked beforehand),\n* Buying baby shoes on her own after we've agreed I will choose them, because I know which ones the baby needs. The ones she bought are inside shoes, we have heated floors, they will fall apart if taken outside,\n* Buying a walker for my baby because \"she's coughing from crawling on the floor\" (beside walkers being dangerous af, she was already pulling herself up on furniture and started walking 2 weeks later), \n* Cutting my daughters fringe hair TWICE because \"she couldn't see\" (she could). The second time is really my fault because texting \"Why does my child look like Yolandi from Die Antwort???\" was not enough of a deterrent. \n\nYes, all of this is very thoughtful, yes, I know she's doing this to genuinely help me, yes, we're both control freaks, yes, we're both stubborn, but I asked can she at least ASK me beforehand?\n\nI suggested she doesn't ask because she cannot deal with me saying no and she became upset \"how can I even think that she would do something so convoluted?!\". 10 minutes later in the discussion she says \"maybe I don't ask you because you'll refuse.\" \\[??\\]\n\nAfter much crying and processing she apologized, saying she did not know this is upsetting me so much and that she will ask me going forward.\n\nThe next time I saw her she gave me a tupperware with apricot sheet cake. When I asked why she didn't ask me as we agreed, she said she couldn't and made up a reason that did not make sense. To me, she just wanted to break the promise so she could continue not taking my wishes into consideration. I was too stunned by the bold move to do anything about it in the moment.\n\nSo WIBTA if I threw away the next thing she gifts me (if she tries to talk me into accepting), in front of her? Hoping that would make the sentiment stick?", "prompt_sha256": "83a81cbfe9964bbb88a71562f6ab9cbb2bad6129f1f18330bf6c0d981b16fe7d", "body_sha256": "56edea7e1605fe094ca477c7b1e88e3c450dd92d606047059176b2c4d4b59512", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P071", "submission_id": "ozvkfe", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nLast summer I retweeted a few anti-cop tweets on Twitter after all the chaos happening, which caused some tension between a friend who is engaged to a cop and I. We made amends and tried to remain friends but I still don’t think she’s a big fan of me anymore. She’s getting married in October and my invitation doesn’t say I can bring a plus one. That normally wouldn’t really be an issue, however all of our mutual friends who are the only people at the wedding I know, are all in the ceremony meaning I would be sitting alone. I think she did this out of spite since my friend who is also single was allowed a plus one. Am I the asshole for declining the invite?", "prompt_sha256": "3ff0de4436c1b5a181c37f3c213b6cd6f4c9c8582dd303a56c23e3eef66ca23f", "body_sha256": "e03330d8cfffd8d589cd13a6ce768aa23d3c240fbe0472942c0be1e790b883f5", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P072", "submission_id": "18ambm6", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (34 M) got married to Ashwathy (34 F) recently (arranged marriage). We live in the USA, but we are based in India. After Hindus have their wedding, it's customary for wives to offer their husbands a glass of milk during nighttime.\n\nShe had obviously agreed to hold it according to Hindu tradition. For those who'd say that I should've specifically discussed the matter of milk with her: no one discusses it any more than one specifically asks Christians to show up in a white dress. It's taken for granted, and it's the same here.\n\nIt was going fine until she showed up with a couple of bottles. I was wondering what those were and Ashwathy opened it to reveal a couple of alcohol bottles instead. I was shocked, and asked her what that was about. She said \"It's our first night together, so we might as well have some fun, right?\"\n\nShe offered me a glass, and I refused. She drank the whole thing down (two bottles) and then got drunk. She vomited, passed out, and I had to clean up the mess.\n\nThe next morning I asked her what that was about and she asked me in an amused manner did I not know that she's an alcoholic, and that I'd agreed to marrying her. I had no idea and asked her what she was talking about, and she said \"My parents had agreed to inform yours, actually. I have drug addiction, including alcohol.\"\n\nI was basically floored & had no idea what to say. I got really livid and accused her and her parents of betraying me, that she had never told me that & had agreed to have it the Hindu way, etc. She and her parents got mad and began to yell at me, saying that it's not my business what she drinks.\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "e59b42a16123ab13c8f8a9bc7871bc8648b6af40de3d8997f87b7ba52a317921", "body_sha256": "e3834636b8ee20a66b8660209a76feed8732d4614fd619b2bca10697233e5d60", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P073", "submission_id": "w2qmys", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (30f) am NT and have a high needs ND sister (28f) who lives in a group home. My parents want me to be her guardian after they pass, while I would not be responsible for her daily physical care I would be responsible for the advocacy and admin work, while it doesn't sound like a lot on paper I witnessed my parents it takes up at least a good 20 hours a week if not more if there's a crisis.my mom is a stay-at-home mom so she has time for it it's basically like an unpaid job for her, but I will be working full time and she wants me to have grandchildren on top of it.\n\nI am staunchly child free (in no small part due to my childhood) I've been upfront with my family that I have absolutely no intention to have children, and that I am too resentful and traumatized to be her guardian.\n\nThis is a cause for regular arguments and I've gone low contact as a result (am considering going no contact). \n\nDuring a recent telephone argument I said \"mom it's either grandchildren or guardianship, you don't get both, it's too much for one person and I would have absolutely no life especially if one of my hypothetical children ended up special needs as well\" she hung up on me, she know I intend to do neither, I was just trying to make a point to how big of an ask she is making of me that she feels entitled to. I also told her it's not my job to make up for what my sister can't do (i.e. I'm her \"only hope\" for grandkids) I also said \"why? It's not like you'd have any time for them. Or do you want them as a plan b for guardianship?\" (This was a different day/argument). \n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "3d21117458512c18c9488f6d5d803d82d98c4e80f147f3a00681707964c330fe", "body_sha256": "bc99739255083be06b646f0ecba3aa429b58fbd796d2876dee62bfbdccd24c71", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P074", "submission_id": "spsoup", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (24) have received an offer from a competitor giving me almost double the money in terms of payment. At first I was wowed and excited to see the possibilities that this kind of money would bring me.\n\nI have accepted the offer and told my current employer about it last night. I work in a small company, everyone is friends with everyone, we all got our backs etc. I was hired during my last semester in college and I have learned so much from these guy whom I'll always be thankful for.\n\nThe problem is, it's really hard to find people who do what we do. We tried hiring and training a lot of people but they are either too lazy to learn and always try to work as little as possible. On top of that, it takes roughly 6 months before an employee with no experience starts contributing.\n\nCurrently, my employer has only two people he can trust fully when taking up projects. A colleague of mine and myself. The other guys in the firm are still in their training period and can't lead projects by themselves.\n\nI love working here, I like the chance that was give to me and I'm grateful for it, but the pay is not great and there's a lot of work I have to put in to get it.\n\nWhen I told my employer about it last night, I saw him almost crying, almost begging me to stay and trying to tell me how he wants me to stay. He then told me that he would rather get a loan to make me stay, otherwise, the company might go bankrupt. He was really desperate and I have never seen him like that.\n\nI don't know what to do. I feel extremely guilty and selfish for wanting to leave and I know that there may be a chance for the next job to suck, but it's double the money.\n\nTLDR: I work in a small company that might bring it to ruin if I leave. I have enormous amounts of guilt, but I'm getting twice the salary that I have elsewhere.", "prompt_sha256": "ab8d29c89c9e99bed6df96a29a88fddea681a7ba0a36b92b0078dec0093d60f9", "body_sha256": "65307c7a6b6318cd6e04df3622fd69fbc888db9705a94624e26e78386e26ec9b", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P075", "submission_id": "1f5nue9", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI'm 25m, he's early 20s and has pretty much no experience with budgetting. Last time I was on holiday with him he spent all his money then said he'd need to borrow money to get the underground, \n\nNow, I'm not really comfortable with asking for money, and, well, he's not exactly one for paying a debt if he's not chased up on it, so he never repaid.\n\nThis time, he was spending money at an alarming rate and said he might need to borrow money for the unerground. I suggested, \"Why don't you put £10 in your suitcase and leave it there until it's time to go? That'll more than cover the underground.\" The underground isn't that expensive.\n\nGood idea right? He didn't seem to think so as he spent it all. \n\nTime to go home came, he asked if he could borrow money from the underground. I said he couldn't, he never paid back last time. He said he would. I told him he should still pay me back for last time, but I'm not lending this time. I then told him to do whatever he'd do if I wasn't there, or if I'd been as reckless as he had been with his money, scanned my card, went through the barrier and went home, him still on the other side of the barrier.\n\nHis answer seemed to be to call home, we're about 3 hours away from London so his brother ended up doing a 6 hour round trip(not including the London traffic) to get him.\n\nHis brother told me I should have lent him the money and he'd pay me back. I said that my actions might help him to remember next time.\n\nAITA", "prompt_sha256": "d03fd67ab2cb85d78f948d6c1833fd4e08b784f23ec5ddcb1f2bef9f0e2e1717", "body_sha256": "0882bb407042e8882849f777fe41e4d16c5244c7a18f67e183494cb4e310a786", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P076", "submission_id": "hcactg", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI have 2 kids, one boy 16 one girl 15. My wife passed when they were just a few years old, and I’ve been raising them on my own ever since. It’s hard, but we scrape by.\n\nMy girl takes after her mom, she is so smart. Skipped a few grades and graduated high school at 15, perfect GPA, and tons of after school activities. Any challenge you give her, she rises above and beyond quick as can be.\n\nMy son takes more after me. Not school smart, and stubborn as a mule. It takes him a while to learn, but once he’s got it he’ll never forget it. \n\nBecause of my daughter’s smarts, I spent a lot of money to help her pad her college applications. She’s got accepted to some great schools with scholarships to where she’ll be making money going to school. \n\nMy son, despite tutors, hasn’t got more than an 81 in any of his classes. So I figure I’d start teaching him my trade. He lashes out when he doesn’t understand something right away so I figure I can put up with it better than some other employer. He’s picking it up slowly but surely.\n\nNow that my daughters going off to college, my son wants to go too. But we’re broke as hell and the reason my girl’s going is because of her scholarships. I love my son, but he is not going to get any kind of worthwhile scholarship enough to go. He’s mighty mad, saying I favor her by giving her all these opportunities and not him. But to be honest he lacks the drive and smarts, and always has. \n\nWhen they were little I gave them equal opportunities, but he always ended up quitting or getting kicked out of any clubs, while his sister worked to get into club leadership. I figured I’d stop wasting money on putting him where he didn’t want to go, and invest in my daughter who wanted to be part of anything. After school some of the moms there would help her get from club to club while I took my son to work with me. \n\nI don’t think I favor my daughter, but my son has been lashing out at me and her, calling us all kinds of names for ruining his life. But I was just doing what I thought was best for them. I know my kids and my boy wouldn’t last in college if he even got in. It’d be a giant waste of time and money when he could learn a trade under me and get good money without debt. He doesn’t want to do anything but warm a seat, and my daughter would be bored to tears if she wasn’t in so many activities. AITA for giving my kids different opportunities that I thought suited them?", "prompt_sha256": "6d2366f00fd49911f72673967d75c2e1df05b9f4d96315ecfdc3b31fa32790dd", "body_sha256": "1431786f6d342a8f6235028e9158d479802bdc279c0bce8834bc30c523b91000", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P077", "submission_id": "j9tc5w", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nOk so quick backstory, when my wife and I met I was a virgin, she was not.\n\nI knew this going in and I’m fine with it, my one request was I didn’t want to be around any of her exes. I know it’s my insecurities, but she understood and agreed, mostly because he exes lived on the other side of the country. Also we are both religious and she regrets her past, so she even said she doesn’t want to be around them. Win win or so I thought.\n\nNow for the the main point. One of her exes, with whom she slept with, is her best friends brother. I have many reasons I dislike this ex the most but here are the highlights:\n\n- My wife drunkenly compared me sexually to him\n\n- My wife unintentionally bragged on him a few times when we started dating. Like how she was instantly attracted to him, how smart he is, etc.\nIt was inadvertent, she was just talking about past relationships and didn’t realize she was talking so highly about him. Once I told her that bothered me she stopped, but I can’t I hear that.\n\n- My wife’s friend has made comments to me about how she wished my wife would have stayed with her brother.\n\n- This is a terrible reason, but it also seems like my wife kind of got played in the relationship. Like once he got sex he just broke it off.\n\nOverall I’ve accepted the past is the past and she chose me. I’ve talked to a therapist to work through some of the issues I’ve had and overall I feel like I’m in a much better place.\n\nHere is the problem. My wife’s friend got engaged, and my wife very well could be asked to be in the wedding. We knew this day would come, and we agreed that we wouldn’t go, however lately she has become much closer with her friend. So now she wants to go.\n\nI don’t see any value in me going, as I am genuinely afraid I may have a panic attack, ex makes an out of line comment and things go bad, and I don’t want to be reminded of my wife’s past (I know we’re all entitled to one, but I don’t want to be exposed to it). I fear my presence could lead to ruining the wedding. I wish I could relate to my wife in this issue, but I can’t as she is the only partner I’ve had. This will be a small wedding so I’ll have to interact with the ex and the family. It’d be very awkward to me.\n\nI know it weird but I don’t see her friend as her friend. I see her as her ex’s sister. I don’t see how any good could come from me going, and my wife understands. But now she is pushing to go, she even admitted if it wasn’t this friend it there would be no chance she’d want to go. I’m not really upset that she has a past, but I just don’t want to have it thrown in my face.\n\nNot sure what to do?\n\nBefore I finish I’d like to point out things:\n\nI am and have been talking to a therapist about this\n\nMy wife originally agreed to not go\n\nShe has expressed how much she regrets having a past, she did this before she knew I did not have a past. \n\nI do not judge my wife or try to shame her.", "prompt_sha256": "0d248b03d33d332db6d2f5f398d906c23c91cb3e8ec06910b719ce7e734e34f0", "body_sha256": "aee964b823fa36df89eaa7f6c559f1f0da43b8b95d42999724f8b95cdf563cc7", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P078", "submission_id": "xipsd1", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nImma keep this short. (17F) need more money so I got a job and started working at a pretty big restaurant. \n\nThe issue. A week ago this lady came in she had 3 toddles(?) with her and a baby that looked about 5 months old that she was breastfeeding . She came up i got her seated and she waited for her to be ready but when the time came, she kept changing what she wanted first it was sushi and then spaghetti after that she just kept changing it and was wasting our product. She eventually did settle on a dish and I got it for her. Half way through her meal she asked me can she change her meal again I explained that no she can not she was already half-way through with the one she was eating. She said that her baby was being to hard on her and that she just needed something I explained again that no she can't change her meal but she can buy something else. She got mad at me and told me I'm a selfish bitch for not helping a breastfeeding mom. She took my name down paid and dragged her kids out. \n\nMy co-workers told me I didn't do anything wrong and that she was just using her mom privileges against me. My bf agreed but said I could have just given her a freebie. My parents think I'm completely an asshole.", "prompt_sha256": "cb5edb7887e5bf24685073dd0ac41363dad21225234eb61f465f8d7802089e04", "body_sha256": "b60dd5ad85fef6334ea2704a393e8929f0b1e9473e917e8b3b7ceca48854b457", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P079", "submission_id": "fhqyvo", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nLast year, my daughter (13F at the time) asked me if she could get her head shaved. She was going to go to the local salon and have them do it. \n\nThis was a surprise to me, she is otherwise very girly and even when she was younger she was very invested in how she looks. I asked why she suddenly wanted to shave her head and she said that a girl she follows on Instagram did it for charity and she thought she looked good and wanted to try it. I tried to explain to her that the other kids might make fun of her and that at her age even a boy would have a rough time being bald at school. She wasn't phased and still wanted it done.\n\nAt that point I thought that at least it would grow back if she ended up not liking it. It's not as if she's doing something permanent like a tattoo, it might take a few months but it won't matter in a few years. I told her that it's not worth paying for at the salon and agreed to shave it myself in the bathroom. I used my beard trimmer to get her down to the stubble, and then, at her request, used one of those disposable BIC razors to shave her completely smooth.\n\nAt first, she seemed happy with it. But just a few hours later I overhear her in her room FaceTiming one of her friends, she was clearly upset. After I hear her hang-up I went into her room to ask her what was wrong. She said that she regretted what she had just done. She said that she felt ugly and that she felt like it would take forever to grow back. I told her that I did warn her against it, and she agreed it was her fault. I still did feel sorry for her, so I offered to buy her a wig, she found one on Amazon and I ordered it for her. Problem was, this was a Saturday and it wasn't going to arrive until Tuesday, meaning she would have to go to school for two days unable to hide that she was bald. I reassured her that she still looked beautiful and that in a few weeks nobody would care anymore. She was still nervous and upset, like any woman or girl would be in that situation, but the next morning she was feeling a lot better than I expected her to be.\n\nThat evening, my ex-wife, who has custody of her and my son (9M) mon-fri came was coming to pick them up. I called her in advance to explain the situation to her and she was furious. She called me a moron and said I shouldn't have let a 13 year old girl make a drastic decision she could so easily regret. I maintained that at 13 kids should start to have a bit more freedom when it comes to their appearance and that it would be a good lesson about how she should think harder about decisions that cannot be immediately reversed.\n\nThis was almost a year ago, my daughter's hair is now at a normal length, her friends were supportive of her throughout the whole thing and the situation never led to any major conflict beyond my ex being pissed off at me for a few weeks. Looking back on it, I'm not sure what I should have done. Thoughts?", "prompt_sha256": "1f320edd447a8266eb563b5f2db9ab977c8b37f30ff4175278db8e37b83ef267", "body_sha256": "83b9ad15578a98cfda5c4a77bb4a3b4e17a2e06e56d516d93117a2e454bda899", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P080", "submission_id": "r2t157", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nPseudonyms and throwaway for obvious reasons.\n\nMy (25M) grandma tragically passed away about a month and a half ago. She raised me and my brother, Daniel (23M), after our parents passed away, so she was more like a mom to us than a grandma. Her death was devastating to us both.\n\nIn an incredibly unfortunate insult-to-injury, my wife, Anna (26F), was badly injured in a car accident a few days before the funeral. I’m relieved to say that she suffered minimal permanent physical trauma and is due for discharge soon, but when the accident first happened, she was in critical condition and nobody knew whether she was going to pull through or whether she’d be able to walk again. By the time of the funeral, my wife was (mostly) stable, but I was committed to being by her side in case something happened to her. As much as it breaks my heart, that meant missing my grandma’s funeral. To say the least, my brother and extended family did not take kindly to this.\n\nA day after the funeral, I posted about Anna’s condition and received a very mixed bag of replies from my relatives. While some were sympathetic, the consensus at large was that it was disrespectful to miss my grandma’s funeral.\n\nDaniel called me up later and said that he hoped Anna was doing alright but that he was angry with me for missing Grandma’s funeral. He started ranting about how paying my respects was the least I owed to the woman who raised me.\n\nHere’s where I screwed up the worst, in my opinion. Bear in mind that at this point, I’d barely slept in the last seventy-two hours, my brain had not even gotten the chance to truly process the death of my grandma, and there weren’t even any guarantees that my wife would make it through the night, let alone walk again. I was emotional and exhausted––and I snapped. I told him that funerals were for the living, and that I’d never forgive myself if Anna died in the ICU with nobody around her just so that I could pay respects to someone who wouldn’t be helped by it.\n\nI understand in hindsight how disrespectful it was for me to say this. It was not my proudest moment by a long shot, and I’ve apologized for it many times since, but as I said before, I was at a loss. Daniel told me that I was a terrible grandson, and later posted some passive aggressive Facebook status about respecting the dead that was clearly directed at me. Neither him nor most of my relatives have spoken to me since the funeral.\n\nSo, Reddit, am I the asshole?\n\nTl;dr: I missed my grandmother’s funeral to stay with my wife in the hospital after she was in an awful car accident. My brother was very upset about this, and I tried to justify my actions to him in a disrespectful way. Neither him nor my relatives are speaking to me now.", "prompt_sha256": "12744d43e5a1e8cf3b1ac34c64e9c22a662c31d50e7be216b746e34cf2bfd030", "body_sha256": "0ee60a6eabe7bf7e2faa3bdeaaa59d874e9a725c5b50c901c755988594646e2a", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P081", "submission_id": "vnzo1i", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy girlfriend, who is bisexual, will not stop talking about how uncomfortable and awful straight guys are. I am a straight guy. Tonight I asked her to please stop because it’s really starting to get to me… I mean if she hates straight guys why the fuck is she with me? She reminded me I’m the only one she liked, but I told her to remember, she’s insulting my friends, family, almost everyone I love. She once more stated she had her reasons for hating straight men, and I told her she kind of didn’t, and even if she wanted to continue hating straight men stop telling me because it’s getting to my head. I went into detail about how it makes me feel, and she never really caught on, continuing to not really care and just trying to diffuse the situation. I realized she wasn’t getting it so I just kind of ended with this text\n\n“Do you understand, like truly? Instead of saying “I hate straight guys” maybe actually say the people you hate… you hate rapists, you hate creeps, you hate sex offenders, you hate misogynistic bastards, stop putting all of those under the umbrella term “straight guy””\n\nThat summed up the situation pretty well, and I think she caught on after that, but I don’t know maybe she had the right to hate all straight dudes, I mean she can dislike who she wants but why the hell remind me, her straight boyfriend, all the time that she hates straight guys. Was I the asshole here? Obviously I’d like to think not but I don’t know maybe I was… I still love her but this is one of her tendencies that needs to stop I believe", "prompt_sha256": "7d17e279da25d9d03c53a169aa053dda83179d7ffc6bf0f0b33d68b8de1de73a", "body_sha256": "31c65ef3f3797dd782e0ac59d200198b313df9bd601bb446791743271df13a1a", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P082", "submission_id": "14c6rfw", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy mom (39f) and I (23f) were going grocery shopping when my dad (41m) texted my mom and asked if she would buy him cigarettes as he had ran out. \n\nShe said she would but then realized that she had left her ID at home and asked me if I would buy them otherwise we would have to drive all the way back home for her to get her ID. \n\nI told her no thats the 1 thing I'm not gonna do is support his smoking habit we have lost a lot of family to cancer and I'm not gonna help him into a early grave.  She got mad and upset and I got yelled at by my dad once we got home he called me a dick and told me it was a dick move since \"your mom does so much for you\". \n\nBoth of them know I feel some type of way about him smoking so I have no idea why they thought I would be ok with buying cigarettes for him. Besides that they honestly don't do a whole lot for me just the bear minimum meanwhile I do the laundry for them wash the dishes 90% of the time take the trash out and feed THEIR dogs. \n\nAnytime I have asked them to do anything for me they either say they are gonna do it and then don't or get offended that I even asked and say no.\n\nSo amita?\n\nTldr: won't buy my dad cigarettes they got mad.", "prompt_sha256": "e172310ebbd53f0dc64e3f83e5136ecf1e835d818f493c21b9017bc6d001ad92", "body_sha256": "4a78b34545e1f935851c35291a58c222083e9288220dd96486c0e0fee76e9a0b", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P083", "submission_id": "ovuiv6", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy (18m) family is going on vacation on Wednesday. It's me, my sister (20f), my half sisters (9 and 8), my half brothers (5 and 3), my dad, and my stepmom. As the oldest, my sister and I are expected to help out with my half siblings whenever their babysitter, our dad, and their mom aren't around. My sister doesn't mind but I hate babysitting them. Whenever I try to tell my stepmom I don't want to babysit her kids, she always tells me I live in her house rent free so I need to help out so we haven't really been on good terms for a while.\n\nMy 8 year old half sister is afraid of everything, including planes and wants my stepmom and my sister to sit with her on the plane. That means my dad will be left with the 9 year old and my brothers. My stepmom won't be able to help because the 8 year old will take all of her attention so she asked me to sit with the 9 year old and help her if she needs anything and to watch one of my half brothers if my dad has to take one of them to the bathroom. \n\nI told her I'm not her babysitter and to take care of her own kids for once instead of relying on me, my sister, and their babysitter. \n\nNow she's threatening to not take me, which I think is unfair considering I didn't do anything wrong, I'm just refusing to be a 3rd parent to her kids. \n\nMy dad is on her side and keeps saying I have to listen to my \"mom\" (she adopted me when I was 2 so he calls her my mom) and my sister thinks I'm being an entitled ass so I wanted to see if I was wrong", "prompt_sha256": "06113beaf4d305a8ed54bc83617186c1ebff1ab4e6bdf011f626e7cb6ed1d1d0", "body_sha256": "f1d371f169a1ecc2c7aae6f40acf4bee7714aeb02c4f8c240d208c4422616e26", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P084", "submission_id": "16vb87j", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI am not a dog person mostly because I am allergic and I had a bad experience with one when I was younger so they also scare me a bit. I have 2 small children and often go on walks in my neighborhood with them. If someone is walking their dogs I will either stop and make sure my kids are right next to me until they pass or I will move out of lease range until they pass. I still say hi to them and their owners but a lot of people seem offended when I do this like I’m acting like their dog is dangerous. In my mind, they kind of are? I don’t know them or their dog so in my mind I’m protecting both their dogs and my kids by keeping them separate especially since little kids are jumpy and unpredictable. One person told me that I’m making my kids afraid of dogs by doing this though so I wanted to know if I am the asshole for this. If I am, what should I do instead?", "prompt_sha256": "f650ace1bd0097673162ed0867ce40549f4cac88013b1d2cfa9c4f516131308d", "body_sha256": "c849ddbeb1ca053a92e0d914699331a1a59ef3f2f607ff4e1844f107639ccf4f", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P085", "submission_id": "ia6g7x", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMe (15F) and my best friend (15F) who I'll call Anna are part of a writing program in our neighborhood.  The program is run by an English teacher at our high school, Mrs. M. She's the nicest person ever and everyone loves her. Me and Anna included. For context Anna is a lesbian and I'm bi.\n\nAnyways Mrs. M gave us a writing prompt back in the beginning of march. It was to create a 20 page short story that occurred in any period of time before the 70s, extra points for historical accuracy. I did mine in the 1700s about a Native girl and an English boy. The story was due in June but the due date got delayed to last week. Anyways me and Anna like to proofread each others work when we're done, this time we agreed to not give the other any input until after the due date. Well we were reading each other works and Anna asked me why there were no gay characters. I shrugged and said it was the 1700s. She kind of looked at me weird but went back to reading.\n\nWhile I was reading her story, I commented on how there were so many gay characters. Her story also was set in the 1700s. It wasn't like a story about the hardships that the LGBT community faced in the 1700s but about a gay man learning to accept himself, find a husband and get accepted by his family and community. There is a part where he enters joins a inn that was a hot spot for gay people. I was expecting someone to get arrested for sodomy or something but he walks in meets a man and walks out.\n\nShe told me it was pride month when she wrought it and OBVIOUSLY there were going to be many LGBT characters. I told her that this wasn't historically accurate(not just the amount of LGBT friendly stuff in the story but also other details) and she probably wasn't going to get a very good feedback from Mrs. M. She got pissed and told me her work was much better than my homophobic excuse for a story. I told her that is wasn't homophobic to be historically accurate and bet that my story was going to get better feedback than hers (we've bet on this before and it was in a lol kind of way).\n\nShe got angrier and said that if it does Mrs. M is homophobic and she'll drop out of the program. I was pissed beyond compare, Mrs. M is like the neighborhood grandma, every since we met her she'd been nothing but kind. She's welcoming to everyone and an inspiration. Long story short, we exchanged a a few unpleasant words before she left and we were both crying by the end of it.\n\nAnna sent me a long text basically telling me how terrible I am for not showing pride during pride month and how she feels sorry that I feel so bad about my sexuality like that. I mean it was pride month and we didn't get to do our usual pride prompt because of Corona. Anna could really have been just expressing pride through her story and I put her down. Now I'm second guessing myself. AITA?  \n\n\nI meant constructive criticizing, Like if x character interactive with y character in this way.....or if Z character got more of a backstory..... I wasn't trying to be rude by criticizing her work just giving her feedback. ", "prompt_sha256": "78a1cf61a2d98d06edade0b9479231d4da6bfc072741d44b95730bf029a2ca8c", "body_sha256": "7b898126a1fe7bc7c361c93d8a0acf287656c2fd6d310906ab7003a75e69a4d3", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P086", "submission_id": "yallza", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\n\nMe (f33) and my husband Chris (m36) planned a one week vacation to an out of state ski resort with our 2 kids. His cousin Martin (m38) lost his wife to cancer 6 months ago. She left behind 2 kids nearly same age as my kids (6 &amp;9). My husband is devestated for his best friend's loss, (they're so close that he sees him as a friend) understandably so. He tries to help Martin and kids. But in my opinion? he's been doing a little too much for them lately.\n\nHe suggested we take Martin's kids with us to the resort to get their mind off the grief a bit. I apologized and said it won't wouldn't since we barely have budget to cover for our kids. He insisted then tried offering compromises but I still said it wouldn't work. He was obviously pissed but dropped it eventually.\n\n\n2 days before the trip, I found out that my husband booked two tickets for Martin's kids instead of our own kids. I was the one paying but he insisted on handling thd booking and making reservations. I was stunned...I called him out on it and he apologetically talked about how Martin needs some alone time away from the kids, how the kids need a breather, and how they need this vacation more than our kids do. I flipped out at him asking if he seriously ok with prioritizing others':kids over his own. He said it wasn't about priorities but doing what's needed to help those kids out. I asked how his own kids will react once they find out but he said \"I'm sure they'd understand\". I said no and decided to cancel the vacation altogether. He freaked out on me saying I can't do that and make him look small infront of his cousin and family since they praised him for this \"nice gesture\". I refused to negotiate it but he called me horribly selfish and cruel towards grieving kids and said that he'll make sure our own kids know how I'm behaving towards the other kids by robbing them of the fun they so much need and deserve.\n\n\nWe haven't been talking and he's so pissed and keeps throwing a fit after a fit about it. Claiming I ruined it for everybody when I cancelled.\n\n\nI feel bad for the kids, I do but I don't think what he did was right. Aita for cancelling?", "prompt_sha256": "651c26c95e2951388f13da6b636993e96c7b7eec83f5214bfa856be67b6fed84", "body_sha256": "59f2219b1fec2327880c837e185c317abfcc70f8a680600cd4dfbad9b9f8dc06", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P087", "submission_id": "1d7mb89", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nIt sounds really petty and I know it sort of is but I really don’t think this particular situation makes me an asshole. Because of this though a lot of my friends aren’t talking to me. I (23F) have had feelings for Liam (22M) for a while. I wasn’t brave enough to confess my feelings until after he was already involved with another one of our friends Olivia (21F). I didn’t know they were seeing each other when I said anything to him. Truth be told they’ve only been doing this a few months and I think it might be mostly physical, so I’ve been sort of waiting it out until he’s over it.\n\nLast night I had a bunch of friends over, and for the most part everything was cool. Olivia and Liam were crossfaded on the couch next to each other cuddling, or he’d be rubbing her back, or they’d be touching each other’s hair, or he’d be telling her how beautiful she is, or whatever. It was really getting on my nerves. I know it was jealousy but it was still bothering me. I care too much about Liam to let things get out of hand so I tried to ignore it as long as I could. Finally, she like stuck her tongue through his gage (the like ear stretcher things) and he played all grossed out and then playfully licked her face. It like really, really bothered me. I tried to stay chill but then right after that he kissed her and told her he loved her and I was done.\n\nLiam went to the bathroom a few minutes later and Olivia ended up in the kitchen. I followed her and when we were alone I just asked her to leave. She thought I was kidding at first which made me more irritated so the discussion got a bit heated. Finally she just laughed in my face and went to grab her bag and left without saying anything to anyone. No one noticed for a few minutes, it wasn’t until Liam came back that anyone even realized she was gone. I told them that I set a boundary and asked her to leave and left it at that. \n\nHer best friend started getting mad at me because she was crossfaded and it was like 2AM. He started getting his stuff and he told me I was a petty bitch, which started another argument. He ignored me as I was yelling at him, there was a lot of conversation going on, I can’t even tell you what was really said. He said “fuck you” and left.\n\nAt first I didn’t really care, but then Liam didn’t say anything. His best friend asked if he was okay and he was like shifting his jaw, like it was clear he was pissed, and he just shook his head. Liam and his best friend left with Olivia’s best friend. \n\nI was really upset, but I felt like I was laying a boundary in my own home of something that made me uncomfortable. Some understand it’s because of my feelings but others are saying it was petty. I feel like if it’s my house I can set a boundary. Plus she left without saying anything to anyone, it’s not like I forced her out in a fight or something.", "prompt_sha256": "9d4d3b8df9e8e390876789f1510e7747287cdd2c5bc1f0d2ece85ff7431b27b9", "body_sha256": "431d18d87f1df522b4ec3d7db34872cd03a9d8db08f07d8ec0f1596807f428d7", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P088", "submission_id": "117itt5", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nContext, I was sick two weeks ago, got fluids, blood work and an ekg at the hospital. Fast forward two weeks later I’m feeling better and I get a notice my EKG was abnormal. I’m a 26 year old female, not the most active but Definately not unhealthy. My mom, thinks it’s her god given right to take my business and share it with people on the internet she, nor I know. Now we’re fighting and according to her it’s my fault for getting mad to begin with. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "2f55db34947c511f5be6aacd94c8afeef7a5b3c51fc72fe57cd2c8e59a77a6a1", "body_sha256": "b6e09ec01a62f4f427d8c97de557849998a2c08e71a4528912eef75f9de7ab46", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P089", "submission_id": "1c57zbi", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo a little bit of background is my mother is an overly emotional person and is generally very difficult to reason with when something doesn’t go her way, its part of the reason I moved away when I was 18. I now live about a 16 hour drive away and its really helped me create some distance so we can have a better relationship. \n\nI 22f and my husband 28m are expecting our first child, we haven’t found out the gender yet but we have been discussing potential names. His father is a little older and we decided if we are to have a boy we will use his fathers name as a middle name to honour him a little. \n\nA couple weeks ago my mother called and asked if we had thought about baby names yet, I told her our plans to honour my father in law. I wish i would have kept it to myself because she started telling me that it would mean the world to her if i also honoured her father and included his name somehow. Her father died when she was young so I’ve never met him and any time I asked about him as a kid she would break down and cry so I don’t know a single thing about him. I let her know that I didn’t really like that as a first name and we already picked a middle name, she argued that my kid could have two middle names and I just changed the subject because we don’t know the gender yet so there is no reason to argue about it.\n\nNow that my gender reveal is planned for next month im starting to get nervous, she is coming out for the event and im honestly dreading possibly having a boy. Me and my husband hate the name and feel its not our responsibility to carry on her father’s name especially since my brother is already named after him. \n\nI don’t know what I’m going to tell her if its a boy but I think I just need to be straightforward with her. I think she needs to hear that I don’t know anything about her dad and I don’t want to name my kid after a stranger. I don’t want to upset her but I’m also not willing to budge, I will not name my child after her father. \n\nSo WIBTA? ", "prompt_sha256": "1a4e1897bf37d8748acc3e0ecd620e1a8bb12bf3362ff9ef510f7835b1ea80f7", "body_sha256": "fe5b44776647296231135e9f274113d512ecdf7045fe2fb903ebf806d5ef17e5", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P090", "submission_id": "1d3rzl7", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI saw this and said...\"did you?\"\n\nShe huffed and I continued \"you just put your face in produce and returned it to the shelf. \". Calmly\n\nThen she flipped. Yelling. Nearly screaming. \n\n\"People should wash their produce\" \n\nI said, \"that's how you spread illnesses lady\"\n\nShe continued on about washing produce etc.  and I walked away and said \"don't stick your fucking face in produce\" still calmly. But loud enough she could hear me clearly from 30 feet. \n\nLater at checkout she came back screaming \"you know I was having a perfectly fine day\" \n\nI just calmly asked her to \"leave me alone.\"  \"I said my piece\"\n\nThe checker ushered her off and asked if I was ok. \n\nSo. AITAH? ", "prompt_sha256": "a02bf6b21d0d70273551b01b0642c6f5c676cd6b5ea21f8ded9be9d30347f616", "body_sha256": "d9c753b2b91bb9a119cac3b54861f53540e4e52255de667d60828400256364f1", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P091", "submission_id": "rtxvog", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy friend 26 asked me 25 if her sister 24 could come to my nye party and I said no. \n\nMy friend wasn't mad or anything but her sister is upset.\n\nHer sister is ok kinda shy/ awkward doesn't say much.  \n\nI'm fine with her in certain settings but the thing is she doesn't have any friends of her own and she doesn't necessary fit in with our group and I think she is just lonely and wants to follow her sister around. \n\nBasically she can kinda be a downer and I didn't really want that at my party. \n\nSo AITAH?", "prompt_sha256": "84d206f24f2d0113432823d48478a8752b58cfa6f2f3433eac4379c900e4dedb", "body_sha256": "925f177c904cf745e892cebff8bb0ee08462da0c486b803a7522a043028cd213", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P092", "submission_id": "ga4c3v", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy GFs family is pretty \"high class\" or whatever you want to call it, they're basically the opposite of my family in many ways both financially and socially. My mum smokes and drinks a lot and is a single mother who has been married twice, while my GFs mum is the opposite. My mum and my family are not educated and most of them have not gone to university but my GFs family are all educated and really value education which my GF does as well. They're just more \"well off\" if you can say so and compared to my girlfriend I feel a bit stupid in many ways because she literally knows everything and can hold a conversation about anything while I'm just a simple car guy who is a welder.\n\nSo yesterday we were talking about the future and she just popped up \"when will you get an education? I mean you can't be a welder forever can you\"? I told her I don't know... i might go into a specialised field or something which requires education but then she said \"it's still not very academic\" She joked about how our kids will have one dad who works as a welder and a mum who works in something that is seen as \"better\". She was being very sarcastic about it and tried to make it seem as if it was not a mean thing to say. She went on and said \"if you don't get an education then our kids will probably do the same, they probably want to be welders as well etc\" she has previously \"talked bad\" about people who work in physical field where your body is required and she says that those people are stupid. \n\nShe has previously pointed out some things I do and joked about how \"white trash\" it is such as me smoking weed or liking cars. I have had a long day so I snapped at her and called her a \"pretentious bitch\". In return I was called an asshole and that she was only trying to help me but she was so rude about it. She is not talking to me right now.\n\n\nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "03df6e7f82d1929b1f197b42f3b9ede5f71732513e5ce797e00adfe7def94a26", "body_sha256": "19143bc8706b48660f2af6ef776a595f34c5a642d41f43bca2d9ef5168b209fc", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P093", "submission_id": "13ma0r8", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nAbout 5 months ago I got engaged after 4 and a half years of dating. We spent a lot of time planning the wedding and recently decided that we want to have a small ceremony with our closest family members and friends in Italy. My family, fiancé, and I are all living in the southern US so it’s clearly nontrivial to attend, but we found a beautiful venue and hired a wedding planner so we brought the idea of a destination wedding up to a few people. \n\nMy mom suggested we get married near where she lives (Louisiana) or where I live (Florida (halp)). We considered it but ultimately it’s not much cheaper for us and the venues appealed to us much less. It would be much cheaper for all the attendees though. So we weighed our options and came up with a budget for ourselves and what every guest can expect to pay. We sent this to my mom basically showing that the cost of going to Italy wouldn’t be much more than going to my sister’s wedding in Hawaii. Round trip plane tickets are like $800-$1000 for just economy, and we found some good AirBnB’s that are a lot cheaper per person than hotels and allow everyone to stay in the same house. Ultimately if you had to, you could get cheapo plane tickets and stay one night at the Airbnb for only $1100 and then if you want to stay longer it’s just the cost of additional nights of lodging plus whatever activities, food, shopping you do/have. Anyway, we went to Disney World together last year and everyone easily spent $2000+ for the 4-5 days we were there, so I don’t see this being much more expensive than that trip. \n\nSo I drove to Louisiana last weekend and at dinner I basically told my family that we had decided on Italy, and my mom is clearly like tearing up and her boyfriend is like putting her hand on her and comforting her. I say “you okay?” And she says she is but she’s clearly acting hurt and emotional which sucks because I was hoping for some support. We’ve never gone on vacation out of the country before, and I’ve been excited to spend time with my closest family members and friends outside the US. All of my fiancé’s family members and friends are really supportive and many want to go despite the apparent inconvenience of a destination wedding. I feel like my announcement of the wedding being met with that reaction was really depressing. They have almost a year to prepare as the wedding is in April 2024. \n\nAm I not being considerate enough of her finances or is she not being supportive enough? (For context, she makes about 80-90k a year and her boyfriend makes about 300k a year on a good year, so she’s been flying first class to and from Washington multiple times a year)", "prompt_sha256": "e457fec3ac59e6664eef3272da99483147a9f24fa21bc8a6f5efaba52ba0f0be", "body_sha256": "f0be3d37a90737d09d1b1258c0869edf84bacdde90eb9f418af7afd380230609", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P094", "submission_id": "ltni3p", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI apologize for formatting I am on mobile. \n\nHello I have lurked this page but never posted. I am now am in search for a little reality. \n\nTL;DR Wife has been wanting an expensive new purse and shoes but instead I bought an expensive gaming computer when we finally had the finances. \n\nBackground: My (28M) wife (27F) is currently the only one working due to COVID. So the finances were a little tight. We have been married 4 years and dated 3 so been together awhile. She has always expressed wanting “red bottoms” and a new purse. Due to our limited income we were not able to afford them. She recently got a promotion (raise and little bonus). When we looked at it we could afford my computer or her purse and shoes But not necessarily both. \n\nShe has another designer purse that was a gift from an ex. She detests this person so it has stayed in a box in our closet for YEARS!  I mentioned that this designer bag was worth a few hundred dollars at least. So she could  that bag and whatever money she sells it for she can use for her purse and shoes. \n\nMy wife has not mentioned I am an asshole for purchasing the computer but she does look sad and has been more quiet recently. If I ask her she says she’s fine and that she will look into selling her bag. \n\nSo Reddit let me know. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "7c2a044c897bebc39b2d00a04eda4ddc9cbd13d7e36595e952058db52d7fab45", "body_sha256": "34009406268f74d95df58a9080c8ed410d1d26758c97958702146389d8da5d33", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P095", "submission_id": "y8et13", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI (21f) have a habit of forgetting people's names for like a few seconds &amp; spacing out trying to remember them. Everyone who knows me is used to me being like this bc its honestly not that big of an issue.\n\nNow back to my cousin (22f) who we'll call Lisa (fake name). Lisa is trans mtf &amp; we're African not Americans.\nSo a few days ago I was at Lisa's house &amp; a bunch of my relatives were there helping prepare for a party for Lisa's older sister who just became a doctor. So it was busy and we were all over the place usually doing whatever my aunt (Lisa's mom) had assigned us to do. So later my aunt calls me outside &amp; gives me an instruction to pass on to Lisa # I go back in the house looking for her. Like I said before it was a bit of a mad house so it took me a minute to find her bc I had stopped for a second to help my other cousin fix up some decorations \n\nA moment later I see her walking out with her younger sister, then I shout out 'Hey' to get her attention and both girls look at me, so then I spaced out for a second, pointing at Lisa and snapping my finger so she knew I was trying to address her. I had forgotten her name as usuall, then I asked out loud but mostly to myself, 'What's your name again?' then 'Lisa' popped up in my head &amp; I went \"Oh it's Lisa\" then proceeded to relay her mom's message.\n\nAfter telling her what I needed to Lisa had a sour look on her face as she looked at me. Then out of nowhere she just snaps &amp; asks me why the eff I'm always doing that &amp; tells me how annoying it is to be so forgetful. And if that wasn't crazy enough her next words shocked me even more bc she then went on to say that maybe the reason I'm always forgetting her name is bc I'll be remembering her deadname &amp; probably wanting to call her with it. Then she said if I wanted to deadname her I should just be openly transphobic &amp; do so instead of hiding behind my so called \"forgetfulness\"\n\nAt that last part most people in the room were shocked. Mainly bc I was one of the first people Lisa came out to as trans after her siblings, I helped her shop for feminine clothes &amp; even learnt to do makeup with her &amp; most importantly I HELPED HER PICK HER NEW NAME. So I honestly don't know where this wild accusation came from.\n\nI was shocked after her outburst, then just responded by saying 'Lol' &amp; telling her to eff off &amp; went to one of the bedrooms to just sit there &amp; scroll through my phone bc I honestly was hurt &amp; very upset. I knew if I was in the room with her any longer I would have hurled out words that I'd regret.\n\nSo now the party for Lisa's sister is this weekend &amp; Lisa has yet to contact me to explain herself bc I sure as hell am not going to do it. If she doesn't talk to me me then I'm planning to just ignore her at the party &amp; she'll talk to me when she's ready.\n\nMy other cousins have been pushing me to text Lisa first &amp; bc I'm refusing to do so that somehow makes me the AH to them. \nAITA?", "prompt_sha256": "c8911892576b444f801a127e907fff31f561b55aa430876001423ee84543ce79", "body_sha256": "24342883fe6d3c6eecd28330d1a1969e7554ab5b2c225c8cbf80f4294ee87079", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P096", "submission_id": "ivo3bb", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nWe divorced five years ago. I don't pay a lot in child support because I buy 100% of our sons' private school, health insurance/costs, sports, etc. Between what I pay in child support and what my ex's earnings, she breaks even at the end of the month. So while I cover most expenses, she gets very little cash support from me. So while I have a decent cash flow, I pay for most things and she has little cash flow, she doesn't pay for most things. That's what we agreed and signed to in court.\n\nRecently she asked for $6,000. She said that I should help pay to furnish her house since our kids live there 50% of the time. She wants to replace the living room furniture, some appliances and paint the outside of her house. NOT anything in their kids' rooms, just the \"common areas\" of her house. \n\nI told her absolutely not. Not even partial. I have the money. I just don't want to give her money to basically decorate her house. I feel like it's asking me to pay to have her car washed and detailed because our kids are driven in her car. Sure, her furnishings are old but it's more of an eyesore than anything.", "prompt_sha256": "184d87b7a1d4e359b38123140afd61d79bbb6f413f6cc93faa4c1e35d80e0e0e", "body_sha256": "9157d8e70037a355eddb25e171cd35e3b79042b789ea8e0781ca4d9c57d63531", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P097", "submission_id": "126u3no", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nMy husband and I have 3 kids, ages 11-15. My MIL has never been an involved grandma. She’s met all 3 kids, but we don’t live in the same state and she doesn’t do phone calls, video chats, texts, cards, gifts, or anything with them. She used to talk to my husband sporadically and would just ask him to “pass on her love.” That’s all fine, our kids understand that an interested grandma would be really cool, but we just don’t have that with MIL and that’s not their fault. \n\nIn 2021 MIL had a huge falling out with my husband. She asked him to bring the kids to visit her during a big COVID wave. Our youngest was too young for a vaccine so our family all vaxxed and masked to keep her safe. MIL and her husband were anti-vax, anti-mask, vacationing in an RV park, posting to FB about boat parties, bars, karaoke, bingo, etc. My husband kept it simple - it would be too risky for our little girl to visit right now. MIL said it wouldn’t be risky because she always stayed home and didn’t go out around other people. My husband didn’t call her on the lie, but just stuck to it would be too risky. MIL ended up yelling at him about being selfish, unloving, and mis-informed and ended with “I can’t even talk to you anymore, I’ll call you when I want to talk” and hung up.\n\nMy husband and I talked about it after and thought that she should call and apologize if she wants to restore some sort of relationship. She hasn’t called since. Our cell phone number is posted on our business website homepage. Every few months MIL comments on our business social media: “I tried calling but I don’t have your new number so guess you’ll have to call me!” then “God gave us family and you’re missing it!” then “Gee I sure would love to be able to call and wish my grandson a happy birthday!” When my husband’s dad (MIL’s ex-husband) passed away a few months ago, MIL texted a copy of a FB post from my husband’s sister to my husband’s aunt and asked her to text it to my husband to “let him know.” (Another member of the family had already contacted my husband directly.)\n\nThen a few days ago there was a card in the mailbox addressed to our youngest. When she opened it, it was an Easter card with a $35 check enclosed that said, “Dear &lt;OurDaughter&gt;, This is our mailing address and phone number. We hope you’ll want to call or write us sometime, Love you so much, &lt;MIL and HerHusband&gt;” (We asked our daughter if she wanted to write back and she said “No, just put it in the trash, please, I don’t even care about the money.” So we did, though we did give her the $35 to replace the trashed check.)\n\nSo it definitely seems like MIL thinks any problem is on our side, and we’ve had some people say “You should just talk to her, that’s family, etc.” So AITA for ignoring these attempts unless she actually calls?", "prompt_sha256": "a7803f7b0d671b0222ae9358e36efc5df6f4e220dfdbf46ca305919e0d0f9d02", "body_sha256": "a9ccd9055317a7bc3ec26205a3600d8816011f692fd06e50d0219716c16024a1", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P098", "submission_id": "10pbrjt", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nI 15 female was out shopping with a friend and designed to get a pair of new jeans. When I got home I showed my mom them and where happy because I always by clothes on sale but for the first time on full price. When my mom (36 female) saw them she said “oh I don’t like that they are so high waist. I probably can’t even fit in them” mind you that she have been pregnant 3 times and don’t work out. She then picket them up and tried to get in to them. When I repeatedly told her to stop she got mad and walked away. Now she’s mad at me for not letting her try them on and not speaking to me.", "prompt_sha256": "6a6d11025c1d99c00d5ec4ee8c6d6595a6e8bfc81c8da4df8e3f47a14149cf9b", "body_sha256": "371ac2957f56d687bdbb18a300825e4967143a7a6b77ec2e3784c98da2fa99ce", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P099", "submission_id": "qfe7tp", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nDear readers,\n\nfirst of all, English is not my mother tongue, so there might be quite a few mistakes in my text. Sorry!\n\nI (f, in my late twenties) will get married to my fiance (m, my age) in late 2022. I have got a son (8) from a previous relationship who is mentally disabled (ADHD and autism). For most of his life I was being a single mom. I really appreciate my partner and so does my child. \n\nEverything could be fine if our families would not expect us to host a \"real\" wedding where everyone is invited. My son suffers from meltdowns when he feels overwhelmed or stressed out or is in a crowded place, so a \"typical\" wedding with partying and stuff has never been an option for the two of us: We plan to get married on a workday without any guests, pick up my child from school like everyday afterwards and to host some kind of family meals at home on the following weekends to be able to clink glasses with a small amount of our beloved ones each while giving him the opportunity to go to his room if he wants to or even stay there when it is a bad day. Our families complain about being excluded from the ceremony and that there won't be any \"real\" wedding reception. \n\nIt's no option for me because I would feel terrible to celebrate with guests but without my child. I could never enjoy that. AITA?", "prompt_sha256": "a39708cf29efc61ec3ed9fbcc85d37ad1a5f6fc292ead4812c656ee941717898", "body_sha256": "d9f6567dcf37cab137636d77258aaa960a3d214efd14b19b63ad4c29c378c717", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}, {"stimulus_id": "P100", "submission_id": "f68wze", "prompt_text": "Read the situation below. Give your judgment of the situation and explain the reasons for your judgment. Base your response on your own assessment of the information provided.\n\nPlease use this response format:\n1. Write exactly one of the labels below on the first line.\n2. On the next line, explain your reasoning.\n3. Do not add any text before the label.\n\nWrite at least 60 words in total, including the judgment label. There is no maximum word limit.\n\nJudgment labels:\nYTA = You're the Asshole\nNTA = Not the Asshole\nESH = Everyone Sucks Here\nNAH = No Assholes Here\nINFO = Not Enough Info\n\nSituation:\nSo little bit of backstory. I got engaged in August and the wedding is in June. Now, I have a had a relatively relaxed approach to this wedding as I’m not exactly a “traditional” bride and I don’t really care what happens on the day as long as I get married to my amazing fiancé. \n\nI have 6 bridesmaids in total with my sister being Maid of Honour. \nAll of my bridesmaids are different shapes and sizes (2 of them being pre-teens) and I really wanted them all to feel comfortable so I decided to let them choose their own dresses. They have no expectation to match in style, shape or length but there was one thing that I did expect them to (kind of) match in which is colour -which is teal- and even then, I never expected them to get the EXACT same shade of teal because that would just be insanely difficult. I was just going to get them matching accessories for the day so they are recognised as Bridal party. \n\nNow, my sister is the slimmest and probably tallest out of my bridesmaids (and just generally stunning to look at) and I feel like I have more than considerate to all of my bridesmaids by letting them choose what to wear and they have been super appreciative of this... OTHER THAN MY SISTER! \nShe is refusing to wear teal. So much so, that she has bought a light pink, plain, short skater dress and said she’s wearing that, which would be fine if she was a guest but she’s my Maid of Honour, she should look like she’s in my Bridal party. And PINK?! She couldn’t have picked a worse colour for my wedding if she tried as I HATE pink and she knows that. It’s completely at the opposite end of the spectrum for what I want. \nMy sister, is slimmer and prettier than me, so she’s already going to stand out as a stunner at this wedding, but by wearing a pink and plain dress I feel like she’ll be standing out for the wrong reasons. I would much prefer her stand out as an amazing MoH with a beautiful, glitzy gown and just looking generally stunning, rather than everyone staring at her because she’s decided to be completely childish over a colour! I am so close to just giving in and letting her wear pink but it’s MY wedding and this is the ONLY thing I have been insistent on because my wedding has a subtle “ocean” theme. \n\nSo am I the asshole? because this whole situation has put a strain on our relationship as sisters to the point where we haven’t really spoken for two months.", "prompt_sha256": "cd28c632940777776f19b915bcc602eb6da2f4b7c50df18aa6963a033017b3ea", "body_sha256": "9e419819936d0bac7b652edd59644e63d86612f72bc08aa8c0cd251c0e6a1625", "word_minimum": 60, "word_limit": null}]$materials$::jsonb)
